insert into public.sections (id, day_id, section_order, title, content, minutes)
select
  'a16c51d1-7249-4cea-afa8-6e5b8b0b9c2f'::uuid,
  d.id,
  1,
  $d1ens1title$Opening Meditation · Anapanasati and Sahasrara$d1ens1title$,
  $d1ens1json$["Welcome to the 561st day of the Jnanodayam programme conducted by Quantum Life University. From today, for the next ten days, Navaratri will be kept, and on the tenth day Vijayadashami. Each of those days begins here. It is the fortune of this gathering that the founder, Dr Newton, comes and gives the message. As on every other morning, the session opens with meditation: forty to forty-five minutes of practice, and at the end the Sahasrara sankalpa, the resolve offered at the crown. A few minutes after that, Dr Newton is welcomed, and the knowledge he brings is received.","Settle for Anapanasati, mindfulness of breathing. Close both eyes. Join the fingers. Cross the feet. Watch the breath as it happens of itself. If thoughts arise, smile a little and bring the attention back. A gentle music plays behind the silence, to help the attention return. For these forty minutes sit in a steady, comfortable posture. Be still. In this present moment, keep the attention on the breath.","Then, for about five minutes, offer the meditation and the sankalpa for the welfare of the world. Draw the resolve toward the Sahasrara pyramid. There is a light of knowledge in all of us. Let this Sahasrara kindle the inner knowing of humankind. The pyramid is being raised by that resolve, so that it may serve everyone. Soon, the sankalpa says, we should see it in physical form, sit within it, and meditate. Take the attention to the top of the head and experience the power of the Sahasrara.","By the collective resolve of everyone here, look with the divine eye and see the pyramid coming into being. With its coming, an exalted power abides. Many are becoming knowers of the Self and knowers of Brahman. Now release the sankalpa, with faith, into the universe. In this joy, bring the attention back to the breath. Remain in that awareness for a minute, then return slowly to waking: a short countdown, both hands rested for a moment over the eyes, and the eyes opened gently, with a smile.","Welcome again. Today is the first day of Navaratri. Across these nine days, and on Vijayadashami, a rare gift has been given. The founder and chairman, Brahmarshi Chakravarti Dr Newton Kondaveti, guru of everyone gathered, had said the day before that he himself would take all of these classes. To learn from him what Navaratri means, and how a celebration is made with knowledge, is a privilege. Those present are asked to put their cameras on and welcome him with a smile.","He greets the friends of Jnanodayam. Day after day the participation is a fine thing. In the Brahma muhurta, this hour before dawn, the meditation goes on with attention, and Jnanodayam helps each person inspire himself or herself. To meditate together, and to come to know, is the work of the morning. The special nature of these ten days is the first thing to be understood."]$d1ens1json$::jsonb,
