insert into public.sections (id, day_id, section_order, title, content, minutes)
select
  '8375bf28-ba52-4358-aa54-a315d14fb4ed'::uuid,
  d.id,
  2,
  $d1ens2title$Navaratri · Bathukamma and the Girl Child$d1ens2title$,
  $d1ens2json$["These are festivals with an inner meaning. All over India Devi Navaratri is kept, and that meaning has to be known. Otherwise the celebration stays a ritual: some dancing, some joy, and then ordinary life returns. Every festival has a paramartha, an ultimate purpose. The ancestors watched, recognised, and only then set the methods down. For sadhakas, for those intent on knowledge of the Self, for those who meditate, these days are of the highest use. In the Telangana region the same season is kept as Bathukamma.","Bathukamma has a story, and the story is in the Bhagavatam. A soul plan had already been drawn: Sri Krishna was to come as the eighth child and bring Kamsa's destruction to an end. According to that plan they came. The infants were killed by Kamsa. When the eighth was due, Sri Krishna was exchanged, and a girl child was brought to Kamsa instead.","That girl was the Mother of the world, bearing jaganmaya, the illusion that plays through the universe. She is Durga Mata, remembered as Maha Mahamaya, the great enchantment. The story says Kamsa seized her by the feet and tried to dash her against a stone. She was only an infant, and yet the touch of the earth came to her. She asked Mahavishnu. She is his sister, Parameshwari. Why has the earth touched me? The answer is that in the ages to come a great deal will happen on this earth, and the role of Parameshwari will then be very great. Behind the puranic story stands a soul plan.","Parameshwara is the root of creation. Parameshwari is the one who is to complete it, the whole of it. She is the Mother of the world, and she is to come here. Once she has come, the creation is she. The whole of Prakriti, Nature, is she. This is why a story is told behind every festival. Taken with its inner sense, in the way of meditation, it yields something. Taken only as a story, the spiritual knowledge set inside it does not open."]$d1ens2json$::jsonb,
