insert into public.sections (id, day_id, section_order, title, content, minutes)
select
  'c296d5c7-bf82-483a-a897-f1dce9002361'::uuid,
  d.id,
  5,
  $d1ens5title$Sri and Durga · Crossing What Is Hard$d1ens5title$,
  $d1ens5json$["Durga means difficulty. The power that carries us across difficulties, and gives the capacity to overcome them, is Durga Mata. Durgamu is what is hard to pierce and hard to accomplish. On this earth difficulties come to everyone. Sri Ramachandra and Sita Mata had a full measure of them. To have taken a human body is to have come from above, from other worlds, and to find that here there is trouble. The aim is not a life from which difficulty is absent. If our shakti increases, we gain the strength to cross what is hard, however many the forts.","As the nine Durgas, the Mother is decorated afresh each day. Those forms are saguna, Shakti seen with qualities and with a face. For those who meditate, the inner meaning is held: this is Shakti. Without that power, difficulties stay, and they do not end. Increase it by meditation, and any difficulty can be met. Many people say, I must do this, I must do that, and remain dreamers. They make plans and do not acquire the power. Ideas may be there, but an idea manifested here needs the shakti it requires. There is a saying: the anchor stays where it is thrown. We remain exactly there.","The nine days are also the nine months in the mother's womb, set down as a sign. The number nine is a sign. They are called the navavaranas, the nine enclosures. In the body the same number is the navarandhras, the nine apertures, which distract us all the time. The body is a leather bag of nine holes, and we are caught in it. Aham thickens the feeling I am the body. The Shakti that supports the body and drives it is known through meditation.","Practice in this season is of another order. Done on these days it is a hundredfold, a thousandfold. These nine days can bring the fruit of a hundred ordinary days, or of a thousand, according to the quality we bring. There is another reading of the same nine, and it lives in the Sri Chakra."]$d1ens5json$::jsonb,
