insert into public.sections (id, day_id, section_order, title, content, minutes)
select
  '10f8a8df-0463-4d26-a0d8-094439a07a52'::uuid,
  d.id,
  7,
  $d1ens7title$The Practice · Shivaji, Food, and the Tenth Day$d1ens7title$,
  $d1ens7json$["Chhatrapati Shivaji is remembered among us as a hero. In this telling he drove the British out, and the question is how. He received the inspiration of Durga Devi, and through her that Shakti. His guru was a sadhaka, a master of knowledge of the Self and of Brahman, who knew Durga Mata. This is why the vows of Durga Bhavani are undertaken. Different regions of India keep the same observance under different names. These nights are not to be let go.","Each day, a little beyond the ordinary: one further hour of meditation. Reduce the night's sleep by an hour and sit. Wake at three, and in the Brahma muhurta meditate at ease. Less sleep is less tamoguna. Rajas keeps us too restless, too much on the move. Live more in sattva. Food changes for the same reason. People keep one meal, or they fast. A full stomach of rice brings sleep, and that is not the food this season asks for. The food to be taken is the cosmic Shakti. Eat once, ekabhukta, or twice, dwibhukta. The more limited the meal, the more unlimited the power that can be received. Cosmic energy itself becomes food.","Every festival in India was given an inner meaning. The land has been called a punya bhumi, a sacred land, a jnana bhumi, a land of knowledge, a karma bhumi, a land of action, and a land of yogis. The ancestors experienced these energies and only then established the days. What is being kept this October is Sharad Navaratri, the autumn observance. Vasanta Navaratri, in the spring, comes at Sri Ramanavami, and its speciality is different. This season is pushti sadhana, a practice of nourishment: the Shakti taken on the physical plane, so that difficulties can be crossed. Body, mind, and buddhi come into alignment, and the root is caught.","The root of everything is Shakti. The root of Shakti is Chaitanya, consciousness. First the Mother, Parameshwari. If she is held, the Father, Parameshwara, becomes known, because Shakti leads us to him. The Mother comes first. These nine days are a return to her womb. As we grew there, without worry and without anxiety, so meditation takes us back to that condition, and we are born anew. On the tenth day Vijayadashami is celebrated with victory. It is a great celebration. Do the sadhana with a certain splendour. Take this Shakti inwardly as nourishment, and conserve it. Then what is to be gained is gained, and what is meant to come, comes."]$d1ens7json$::jsonb,
