insert into public.sections (id, day_id, section_order, title, content, minutes)
select
  '00f9d1dc-39aa-4596-a90b-6e9ab31e5f39'::uuid,
  d.id,
  8,
  $d1ens8title$The Atman · Kundalini, Vemana, and Three Goals$d1ens8title$,
  $d1ens8json$["Three things are always named in this science. Shakti, power. Chaitanya, consciousness. Jnana, knowledge. The nature of the Atman is the three together. Navaratri sadhana is the sadhana of Shakti. Talk and theory are not enough. Only practice brings the experience. What is that Shakti? It is Kundalini Mata within us. Parameshwari, spread through everything, is in us as well.","Vemana sang it. The Shakti sunk in the muladhara must be seen to rise and float, and seen with intelligence. Brahman in the form of the bindu, the point, must be beheld. Vishwadabhirama, listen, Vema. In this body, at the base of the spinal column, in the muladhara chakra, that Chaitanya Shakti sleeps. We call it Kundalini. Only meditation, and a complete vigilance, wakes it. Then it shines as the radiance of Devi. In a subtle bindu, the reality of Parabrahman is within us. To know this is the sadhana of these nights.","He sang a second verse. The body is a durgam, a fort. Look at it with care, and know it with a clear buddhi. Unable to see the Hari who is inside, people wander. The true fort is this body, because everything here distracts us from our main purpose. The five jnanendriyas, the organs of knowing, and the five karmendriyas, the organs of action, pull us outward. The ears hunt for praise. The eyes must always be seeing someone. The tongue and the skin want taste and touch. We remain in pleasure, and the supreme bliss stays unreached. The fort has to be crossed. Hari and Hara, Shiva and Keshava, are both inside. We wander outside asking where God is, and the time is wasted.","These nine days ask for a full practice. When the hard things have been overcome, Bathukamma is truly danced, and joy overflows. Without Shakti there is no joy. When the cosmic power fills us, whatever is undertaken gets done, because that Shakti does it. So write down three goals. On Vijayadashami some of what is hard is to be crossed. What is troubling you? The Mother who is in us as Kundalini is the one who solves it. The method does not change. Attention on the breath. The breath grows subtler and smaller, awakens the sushumna, the central channel, and introduces Kundalini.","We ourselves make the blocks. A promotion is wanted, or the work should move to its next stage. Financial trouble, once cleared, leaves a freedom in which sadhana is easier. A relationship hurts, and the energy is wasted there. Health may be the thing that is stuck. Set three such goals. Through this Shakti a change comes inside. The angle of seeing changes, and the obstacles leave. The energy of these days is of that order. Parameshwari's look falls on those who meditate. Durga Mata sees that the sadhana is being done well, and she is pleased. She is everywhere as nirguna, in the form of Shakti, and that Shakti is in us. It clears what has to be cleared.","Each day some knowledge is taken, and the more important movement is into further practice. Tomorrow the story of Mahishasura Mardini will be told, and decoded. Each story holds an inner meaning, a yogic sense, a knowledge set inside it."]$d1ens8json$::jsonb,
