insert into public.sections (id, day_id, section_order, title, content, minutes)
select
  '4b4391dd-beeb-4aca-a460-728b7538eac2'::uuid,
  d.id,
  11,
  $d1ens11title$Ellayya · Sleep, Food, and the Three Principles$d1ens11title$,
  $d1ens11json$["Ellayya spoke next. He offered namaskaram at the feet of his parents, of Dr Newton and of Lakshmi, and to the kindred souls before him. While the hymn was sung he had seen the deities: the screen empty, and yet the nine goddesses visible, the song rising from within. Then he asked, as of a doctor, how many hours of sleep a meditator needs.","Three hours or four can be enough, or six. It is decided by the build of the body, by one's condition, by one's life, and a sadhaka comes to know it from within. Too much sleep increases tamas. Too little is also wrong. The right amount is the practice. Ellayya was in Saudi Arabia, rising at about half past two by that clock, bathing, and joining near three. From midnight he was sitting three hours, sometimes four, and he had been in this way since 2019. For the past week he had eaten only rotis, hot food, no rice, where once he ate three or four or five. The chest burned. The head spun. He could not tell whether it was sleep, or whether the practice had become too much.","The body, Dr Newton said, has to be given rest. It must not be overstrained. Parameshwara and Parameshwari are in this body. To strain it is to give them difficulty. Give it the sleep it needs. Eat as much as the hunger is. Do not kill hunger, and do not take even one measure more than enough. Eat a little less than the hunger, and stop. The burning he described is acidity. A heat had arisen. The jatharagni, the digestive fire, had grown excessive, and hydrochloric acid was being released from the stomach because the stomach was hungry. This is not the moment to refuse food on a self-made rule. Eat a fruit, or one roti more. The body should be comfortable. There is a song which says that if, of three rotis, one is left, the eater is a yogi. That condition comes slowly, known from inside, and only then is one roti reduced. It is not imposed all at once. In the same way the inner knowing says how many hours of sleep are enough.","The attention was honoured: another country, the middle of the night, and still he joined. He spoke of eight years in Dubai, and of sufferings from about 2009 until 2019, through which the practice grew intense. In thirteen days, he said, a problem had left him. Since then he had not wanted injections or tablets. It felt wrong, and his Atman was clear, so he had chosen sadhana. Two pyramids had come through the work, and hundreds of people, and elders had trusted him, among them a chance connected with Jyothi and with Vijayabhaskar. When trust of that kind is given, why abandon the practice? He was keeping it at three. The pyramid he had seen was half built, the base ready. It would be complete next year.","He asked about the Trimurti. People speak of Vishnu, Brahma, and Ganesha as uncle and elder uncle. Are there family bonds of that kind? Those three, Dr Newton said, are states, three principles: creation, sustenance, and dissolution, held as representatives, a symbol. They are not to be seen with the sense of difference. Bonds of that domestic sort are not there. We look from a human angle and say that these are brothers, that Vinayaka is the son, that Subrahmanya is the son of Parameshwara. What is there is one God, one Shakti, one Chaitanya, Parameshwara and Parameshwari, present as many forms.","Hari and Hara are one. Shiva and Keshava are not two to be followed apart. That dividing intellect is where we get stuck. It is one figure and the other side of the same figure: approach from this side and one face appears. Meditation makes the oneness known. The divinity in each person is God. Animals are divine to us, and trees, and the whole earth is held as a divine sphere. These nine days, he was told, are for overcoming what he had described."]$d1ens11json$::jsonb,
