insert into public.sections (id, day_id, section_order, title, content, minutes)
select
  '31cda8b1-e7c7-44b2-adfe-6faf4ad99f36'::uuid,
  d.id,
  12,
  $d1ens12title$Questions and Close · Children, Karma, and Tomorrow$d1ens12title$,
  $d1ens12json$["A deputy health education officer spoke next. Dr Newton recognised Nellore, and that the speaker's brother had been his classmate. It was his first time speaking, and the words hardly came. He was serving in that post, and had come to a remote place near Maripadu mandal for his mother-in-law, continuing the work from Duttaluru. He remembered Atmakur, in the early days of Patri Sir, some twenty years before. Around 2006 he had studied in Madurai, and from then had entered meditation. From the age of six there had been hostels and travelling, though he had not known what the restlessness was. Now the wish to know, and to go forward, was strong.","While Harika sang, the verse seemed to move through every organ, and he wondered whether even singers sing so beautifully. He attends the class; when duty shifts the hours, he follows on YouTube. The classes help people like him motivate not only themselves but the society they meet. However busy he was, the knowledge was resonating, and Dr Newton received that as important news: the programme helps everyone. The officer had gathered books on life after death and on the deathless, and was reading them. Even so, the way these masters speak moves the body, and shows, like a question mark, what is not to be done and what is. God is not elsewhere. God is here. He hoped to come with his family. The children had done MBBS abroad and were preparing for the FMGE, the foreign-medical examination.","Lakshmi Kalyani had been waiting her turn. After many months, this was her first time speaking with him. What bond, in earlier births, had she with her husband, or with her children? In this birth the children had become enemies. She had never seen it directly. Even one word would be enough. For months she had held a hard instruction: do not think, we raised them, we fed them, we educated them. However they insulted her, she could see that she had brought it. When they spoke, she would be saying inwardly, this is me. In front of her they said she had eaten while keeping the food to herself. Somewhere she must have failed to serve someone, and it had returned. She knew this. Even so, the sorrow continued for months. Why? She is an actress. Outside, everyone calls her Amma and honours the mother-roles she plays. At home the children do not call her Amma at all.","The answer, Dr Newton said, is already in the question. Which karma of an earlier birth made them enemies? Daughter, daughter-in-law, son-in-law, four at once: what exists is cause and effect. On this earth that is the truth. Without a cause, no effect. When sadhana is done, the knowledge that belongs to it is given, but one has to wait, and to listen. Sometimes a breeze of knowing comes from within, and the angle changes. She had already reported that change. Because I gave this, they are giving it. She could remember a clear case. She had done the same to her own mother-in-law, out of ego, when she was young, and had not known. The same matter was happening now.","One further angle is available. Regard them as gurus — the son, the daughter, the daughter-in-law, and the mother-in-law with them — indirect teachers. Through them, what she has recognised in herself is being reminded. They may speak, and there is no need to react, and no need to suffer. Take it as a lesson. Bring up forgiveness, and compassion, and love the children unconditionally. Unconditional love is what was due when they were small. If they did not receive it, they later say: you were not there, you gave no time, you are always scolding. What was received in childhood is projected again. All of this can clear. Through these nine days, do one hour more. Raise the energy. The angle changes further.","Suppose they were born into her house in order to bring certain lessons. Taken that way, the sorrow goes, and she learns from them. She answered that she had been asking their forgiveness every day, from a year before they left, and still more after they had gone. There is still something to learn. They behave harshly so that the lesson can be taught. When it actually arrives, the feeling of an enemy drops, and they will call her Amma. Patience is needed, and endurance, and forbearance. The sadhana is not to be dropped. She had been waiting to hear this, and her time had come.","Tomorrow morning everyone meets again in Jnanodayam. With auspicious resolves and auspicious blessings, for each person, for the family, for the surroundings, and for whatever work is in hand: may it be accomplished, may the work reach its siddhi."]$d1ens12json$::jsonb,
