insert into public.sections (id, day_id, section_order, title, content, minutes)
select
  'cfe15737-ab66-4372-a176-b98978eb791c'::uuid,
  d.id,
  1,
  $d2ens1title$Opening Meditation · The Empty Vessel$d2ens1title$,
  $d2ens1json$["Welcome to the 562nd day of the Jnanodayam programme. Today is the second day of Navaratri, and once again this knowledge is being received from Dr. Newton. Before that, we have to make ourselves ready. If knowledge is to fill us, we must first become an empty vessel.","Meditation is the way. Let us all practise Anapanasati, mindfulness of the natural breath, for the next forty-five minutes. Sit comfortably in sukhasana, a steady and easy posture. Cross the legs, let the fingers rest together, and if you are wearing glasses, take them off. With a small smile, close both eyes, and simply watch the breath as it is already moving.","By watching in this way we draw the senses inward. Placing the attention on the breath, we become antarmukha, turned toward the inside. These forty-five minutes belong only to the inner journey, with the outer world left aside. When thoughts come, bring the attention back to the breath.","Thoughts never stand in the present moment. We live only in this moment. We cannot live in the past, and we cannot live in the future. Thoughts waste our energy. When the attention is kept on the breath, the energy stays within us, and it gathers in an upward movement. Let us remain in full awareness. Let us be inward. Let us be with the breath.","In the closing minutes the sitting was offered as a sankalpa, an intention for the welfare of all. The prayer was that the knowledge lying hidden within everyone might awaken, and that joy might stir in every heart. The Sahasrara pyramid, the pyramid of the crown, was remembered as a pillar of the lamp of knowledge, a light of knowledge giving direction to everyone. From the four corners of the world many come to this place, sit in meditation, and come to know themselves, receiving atma jnana, knowledge of the Self, and brahma jnana, knowledge of the absolute. Through this modern seat of learning, many are becoming compassionate, and many are becoming wise.","Then, very slowly, the count came down: five, four, three, two, one, zero. Place both hands over the eyes for a few moments, and with a smile open the eyes gently. Welcome back, friends. We have come to the second day of Navaratri.","Everyone in the gathering was invited to turn the cameras on and, with a smile, to welcome the founder and chairman of Quantum Life University, Brahmarshi Chakravarti Dr. Newton Kondaveti. He greeted the friends of Jnanodayam. In these days of Devi Navaratri we are learning the inner meaning as well. The inner meaning has to be known. Only then can these days truly be celebrated."]$d2ens1json$::jsonb,
  4
