insert into public.sections (id, day_id, section_order, title, content, minutes)
select
  '8d8a6923-e91d-47b8-a21b-ccd29c6984aa'::uuid,
  d.id,
  2,
  $d2ens2title$Shakti and Chaitanya · Celebration, Not Enjoyment$d2ens2title$,
  $d2ens2json$["This whole creation is Shakti. Para Shakti, the supreme power, and Apara Shakti, the power that has become manifest, come here as Devi Shakti and create the entire creation. That Parameshwari, the supreme Goddess, pervades the whole universe. This entire brahmanda, the cosmos, is nothing other than Shakti and Chaitanya. In the whole science of this spiritual knowledge there are only two things to be grasped. One is Shakti. The other is Chaitanya, pure consciousness.","Shakti is what we call Mother Parvati. We have given her many names. We call her Durga. We call her Adi Shakti, the primordial power, Para Shakti, Parameshwari. That Chaitanya we call Shiva. We call him Ishwara, Sarveshwara, the Lord of all, Sarvantaryami, the inner ruler of everyone, Sarvavyapaka, the one who pervades all, the Paramatma, the supreme Self. The points to be known are only these two. Yet if Shakti is not known, Chaitanya cannot be known. That is why, in our India, these nine days of Devi Navaratri are kept: so that this Shakti may be known, and so that she may be experienced. The celebration is for that.","Many people do not know the difference between enjoyment and celebration. Enjoyment belongs to a person's own wanting. A desire is there, and when that desire is fulfilled it is called enjoyment. Going out to drink, or watching a film, is taken for enjoyment. Celebration stands apart from that. In the feeling 'I want this, I enjoy this,' a want is present. There is trishna, craving. That is enjoyment. In celebration that wanting is absent. There is ananda, bliss. There is utsava, a festival. However things stand, a person is able to rejoice.","These observances of Devi Navaratri are kept as celebrations. They are festivals. This joy is an all-pervading joy, a great celebration. These are days favourable to the sadhana of Shakti. Whoever is still struggling in life, whoever is still stuck, whoever feels that the answers have not yet come — if that person practises, the fruit of the practice will certainly be received. On these favourable days the power of Para Shakti, of Adi Shakti, is available a thousandfold.","The nature of this energy is of two kinds, and it can be recognised by watching the direction. One movement of energy comes inward. The other goes outward. According to its nature and its direction, the energy we take into ourselves and use within is what we call mahila tattva, the feminine principle. When the direction of the energy is outward, we call it masculine. One is feminine and the other is masculine. The feminine is internal. The masculine is external. These two have to be known first, because today's sadhana is a process we are all going to learn, and it is a practice for every day.","The feminine principle always abides within. What travels outward is the masculine quality, the quality of purusha tattva, the masculine principle. On the physical plane the masculine is always external. That is why women, on the whole, remain closer to their own natural state. They stay nearer the principle of the Self, nearer the heart, nearer intuition. The masculine principle expresses itself outside.","These nine days are the Navaratri of the Mother. All of us are to see only Devi Mata. In everyone, and in ourselves as well, we are to see the Mother. A feeling of samarpana, of offering, is needed. What we practise through these nine days is this: not travelling outward, not scattering the energy, not spending our power outside, but keeping it within. Women and men alike are to do this sadhana. It is a change of direction. For these nine days we do it. Afterwards, whatever is to be done can be done.","Through these nine days we do not scatter the energy outside, and we do not waste it. We contain it within. We let this Shakti multiply inside. It is astonishing, because Para Shakti herself is lying dormant, hidden within us. That power has to be contained. To contain her is to practise with her completely, inwardly, and to bring that Shakti into our experience, into our feeling. From that, something is gained."]$d2ens2json$::jsonb,
