insert into public.sections (id, day_id, section_order, title, content, minutes)
select
  '4f9d0002-b70a-4873-a5cc-3cb64e6cfa66'::uuid,
  d.id,
  4,
  $d2ens4title$The Clod That Stays · Total Acceptance$d2ens4title$,
  $d2ens4json$["The Lakshmi mudra also means this. We are not to scatter our energy outward, nor waste it, nor misuse it. For these nine days it is to be used for sadhana, so that we may become inward. We misuse this energy in many ways, and it is a priceless power. It has to be used well, for the sake of the inward state. Within us many secrets lie hidden. Many great knowledges are there inside. This energy is required if they are to be known. Where there is no energy, we remain exactly where we were set down. There is a saying: the clod stays where it is thrown. It is the same with us.","In life we dream any number of dreams, and in the spiritual life also we dream many. I must reach the ajna chakra. I want the Sahasrara. I must attain the state of the crown. I must obtain the knowledge of liberation. I must cross the round of birth and death. So many karmas lie heavy on me. I must set down my whole burden. Thinking in this way, a great many people remain stuck in the practice. The clod must not be left lying where it was thrown.","This energy must not be misused. Through words, and through our actions, a great deal leaks outward. We keep travelling out. We have to become inward-facing. The more we turn inward and come to feel that Shakti within, the more its direction changes. It begins to travel upward. It should not turn downward and run out into the outer world. It should move buddhi-mukha, toward the awakened intelligence.","Then, through these nine days, one further practice is to be done. It is called acceptance. Every single matter, and every situation, is to be accepted. Our past also is to be accepted. The past has to be accepted completely. If only I had done it in that way, it would have been better. Now I am in pain. I am suffering over the decision I took. In the past it ought not to have happened so. It ought to have been otherwise. The past has to be received whole. It has to be accepted.","In this present also, from the circumstances you are actually in, every single thing is to be accepted. The people who are with you, and the conditions around you, however they are — receive them as they are. Acceptance means to take in, and to agree. Very well. This difficulty is here. This hardship has come. I accept it completely. It has come with a cause.","Nothing is to be refused. No situation is to be rejected. It is to be accepted. If the food you are eating tastes bitter, accept that. You have eaten bitter gourd, kakarakaya, and you do not like it. Accept the bitter gourd as well. Accept whatever is arriving, the sweet along with everything else. There are people, too, who are like bitter gourd. There are people who are sweet. There are people who are salty. There are people who speak with sweetness. Each of them, as that person is, we have to agree to receive.","Drop the expectations. No expectations. They ought to change. They ought to be like this, or like that. None of that is required. Accept, accept, accept. Accept yourself. Whatever state we are in now, that present state has to be accepted. Only then is the next state available. From the state in which we stand, we move into another. This state, though, has to be accepted first. It has to be agreed to completely, and received completely.","This is the practice of these nine days. Write it down clearly. What expectations are still there? What is it you are unable to accept? It may be people in your life. It may be circumstances. Of everything that is happening, what remains unaccepted? For these nine days let us practise acceptance — complete acceptance, total acceptance. From the hour we wake in the morning until we lie down at night, we remain inside celebration."]$d2ens4json$::jsonb,
