insert into public.sections (id, day_id, section_order, title, content, minutes)
select
  'a82b2184-50a7-4d7b-a089-f23d43f04bb7'::uuid,
  d.id,
  8,
  $d2ens8title$Amma First · The Nine Openings$d2ens8title$,
  $d2ens8json$["Through the whole of the day that presence has to be felt. The presence of Devi Mata. Everywhere, Amma is present. Jagadamba is there. The whole of it is the Mother. For these nine days the attention rests with her. Love for the Father may be there, and love for Shiva may be there. The approach begins with Amma. The bond has to be made with the Mother, and a connection has to form with her. We neglect this Jagadamba when we try to arrive at Shiva first. Shakti comes before that. Where Shakti is missing, Chaitanya is missing. The Mother is needed first. She is the one who takes us to the Father. She makes the introduction: this is your father. So each day the presence has to be felt.","Then acceptance, again and again. Let every single thing be accepted. No complaints, and no problems carried as complaints. Accept the past. Accept the present. Accept yourself as you are. Accept each person as that person is. And do not spend the energy in a critical way, going about finding fault. None of that is required, because through these nine days the energy has to be conserved. This is the sadhana.","Spiritually, take it that there is a ladder, and on it many steps waiting to be climbed. If these nine days are done rightly, then by Vijayadashami, the tenth day, that Vijayadashami can truly be celebrated. Wonderfully, a person becomes able to move into another state. Spirituality means obtaining, from the state one is in, a higher state, a different state. That state matters. You become that very Shakti. You become Adi Shakti. When the nine days have been done truly — total acceptance, total surrender, Devi Samarpan, the feeling of offering — the surrender is to this Shakti, and Shakti is not somewhere else. She is within, as Kundalini Mata. The Kundalini Shakti inside us is she herself.","Together with this, the Lakshmi mudra is remembered: the way of sitting, and also the way of seeing. In everyone, see the Mother. See the power of Jagadamba. Whether the one who stands before you has come as a man or as a woman, that Shakti is what created them. This whole Prakriti, the whole of nature, is the Mother. She is in every tree. She is in every animal. This feeling has to live in us. She created the entire world. The pancha mahabhutas, the five great elements, stand under her command as well.","The practice is done in the morning, and it is done again at night. Night means whenever it is possible: from six until seven, or from five until six, or before sleep. Any of these hours will do. Once more, as a reminder to oneself. And the nine, done nine times, is a sign. Why nine? There are the nine months. There are the nava avaranas, the nine coverings, which here are the nine openings. These openings govern the human system: two eyes, two ears, the nose, the mouth, the organ of excretion, and the generative organ. He called them the nine coverings, and they are to be crossed. This Shakti is what carries us across. We are not to remain caught in them.","What is asked is a feeling beyond deha bhava, the identity with the body. I am of the form of this Shakti. I am Shakti svarupa, of the very nature of Shakti. We tend to stay instead inside the other feeling. I am a gross person. I am gross matter. I am this physical body. I am the body. The body, understood rightly, is our house and our dwelling. It is not a mistake that it is here. Our Shakti, though, has also to be known, and for that these nine days of sadhana are given.","Then meditation, two or three times, whenever it can be done. Close the eyes, be at ease, turn inward, and keep the attention on the breath. The breath grows subtle. Every change in the breath is to be noticed. That is the whole of it. Do as much of the meditation as you are able.","And celebrate. Enjoyment is the smaller movement. I want an ice cream; I enjoy an ice cream; I celebrate an ice cream. The third of these is a very different thing, because in celebration the want has dropped away. I celebrate my birthday. Enjoyment belongs only to the physical dimension, only to the physical aspect. We are more than the physical, and that is why the word is celebration. With this feeling the nine days are lived. Afterwards it becomes natural. Every day is a celebration. Life is one great celebration. Every single thing in your life is that supreme bliss. Joy, and joy, and joy."]$d2ens8json$::jsonb,
