  and sec.section_order > 11;

insert into public.sections (id, day_id, section_order, title, content, minutes)
select
  '74e49978-8809-49da-a977-e7ad256f82e9'::uuid,
  d.id,
  1,
  $d3ens1title$Opening Meditation · Sahasrara Sankalpa$d3ens1title$,
  $d3ens1json$["Welcome to the five hundred and sixty-fourth day of Jnanodayam, the third day of this Navaratri series on the essence of knowledge. The two days already gone had taught a great deal. Yesterday the gathering learned how to remain one with that great Consciousness and, from that oneness, how to see this whole world. A sadhana was taken home, so that the principle might be filled into the whole of oneself. Today that practice continues.","As on the day before, the hour begins with meditation. Glasses come off and are set aside. Sit relaxed, on a chair or on the floor. On a chair, cross the legs. On the floor, a basic posture is enough. Let the fingers rest in the fingers. Place the attention on the breath, and, watching inhalation and exhalation, enter the meditative state. A fine music plays. Let it be there, and go on into the practice.","For forty minutes, be with yourself. Do not carry the attention off toward any thought. Watch the breath as it goes in. In the middle a gap comes of itself; watch it. The breath then turns and goes out. Watch the next gap, and watch the outgoing breath return as the next inhalation. If a thought arises, see it and come back to the breath. Whatever experience comes, see that too, and remain as the witness.","The power of the sitting is then turned toward the welfare of the world. A collective sankalpa is taken for the Sahasrara Pyramid: may that Pyramid, for this divine knowledge, for knowledge of the Self and of Brahman, soon take physical form on this earth, and may the knowledge lying within everyone here awaken. Attention moves to the crown. The Sahasrara power is in every one of us. Feel it as a waterfall from the top of the head, through the whole body, into every cell and every organ, joining us, drawing us into oneness.","That oneness is Vasudhaiva Kutumbakam, the earth as one family — every person, every plant, every animal, every mineral. See the light of knowledge in all of them. From this height, see the resolve as already being fulfilled. People come from every place to the Pyramid, meditate, and come to know themselves. The earth is filled with knowers of the Self, and the Pyramid bears a great part in that. With the faith that it is being fulfilled, release the resolve to the universe. In the right way, through the right people, it is coming to completion, and soon. Tathastu, tathastu, tathastu: so be it.","Attention returns to the breath. The last minute, thirty seconds, ten. Five, four, three, two, one, zero. Both hands rest over the eyes for a moment. With a small smile, the eyes open. Welcome back. Friends on Zoom were asked to turn their cameras on and welcome the founder of Quantum Life University, Brahmarshi Chakravarti Dr. Newton Kondaveti. He thanked them, and thanked Harika. A good morning of Jnanodayam: the days of Devi Navaratri were being celebrated wonderfully, each day something belonging to sadhana. This day also, a few things were to be understood."]$d3ens1json$::jsonb,
  5
