insert into public.sections (id, day_id, section_order, title, content, minutes)
select
  '9815fba3-e531-46d0-abac-d17a0f1da5bf'::uuid,
  d.id,
  5,
  $d3ens5title$Three Mothers · Will, Action, Knowledge$d3ens5title$,
  $d3ens5json$["Durga is Ichcha Shakti, the power of will. Mahalakshmi is Kriya Shakti, the power of action. Mahasaraswati is Jnana Shakti, the power of knowledge. Before that Mother we are children. A small child runs and embraces the mother first. She kisses the child, lays the child against her, sings a lullaby. The Mother of the world does the same. These nine days we are to stay near her. When we were small and trouble came, we told mother first, and she helped at once. Father is asked less readily; there is a little inhibition, and he is asked at the end. Mother is the one who convinces him. Dr. Newton told it of himself. As a boy he wanted a toy, and he asked his mother, because asking his father was hard. She spoke to his father, gathered what was needed, and had the gift bought.","Mother means Shakti. Adi Shakti, Para Shakti, has come here as Apara Shakti, in many forms: Durga, Mahadurga, Mahakali, or one name a day — Shailaputri, Brahmacharini, Kushmanda. Each name is one expression of the one Mother. When a problem comes we often run outside. We are to go to our own Shakti and tell her. It is not enough to decide that she already knows. Even hunger has to be said. She might notice of herself and set out the meal. Still, we are to ask. A certain ego says: I will not ask; she ought to know, and come, and give. These nine days, and afterwards, we are to be a child in her lap. She is the power by whom the universes, the galaxies, the solar systems have come to be. Whatever we need, the sentence is simply: Amma, I want this. She is compassionate, and ready. They say her heart moves when a child asks, and she gives it.","With that power of will, the hard blockages are to be cleared — the limitations we are stuck in, the things that repeat, the things that trouble sadhana without our even knowing. Some people have come to a completion in practice. They live mostly in their purpose, spreading meditation or teaching a vegetarian way, immersed in the work. Sadhana is never finished. What has changed is that more of their time goes to teaching, because that completion has come. For the rest of us the blocks do not clear by themselves. Attention is required, the recognition that this block is here.","There is a bird, the ostrich, called nippukodi. When a predator comes it runs, and then hides its head in the sand, imagining that no enemy exists. The enemy is beside it. We do the same. Problems are there, the practice is not happening, and we tell ourselves that we have no blocks. The power of will is not a mistake. Right desires, and right resolves, matter greatly. These first three days are for the blocks inside.","The next three are for resources. Mahalakshmi means abundance, balance, equanimity, the inner store. Confidence is such a resource. If it is there, what you think of, you do. If it is not, you plan and then stop. Divine qualities are to be grown just as the negative ones are real. After that inward abundance finds outward expression, the last three days are Mahasaraswati: knowledge of the Self and of Brahman, received from her. From that mother we learn who we are. Will, action, and knowledge. She is Mahishasura-mardini, the power that brings the asura down."]$d3ens5json$::jsonb,
  5
