insert into public.sections (id, day_id, section_order, title, content, minutes)
select
  '44c8ac92-46a0-42b1-a7f0-56b68cf0dfca'::uuid,
  d.id,
  6,
  $d3ens6title$Suratva · The Nine-Day Fast$d3ens6title$,
  $d3ens6json$["Among musicians, sur means rhythm, and asur means the rhythm has gone. How near we come to ourselves is suratva. How far we go is asuratva. Nearness is the yearning for knowledge of the Self, the Self joined to the Self, and the felt knowledge: I am the Self. Distance is: I am the body, I am not the Self, there is no path. Think that, and every problem follows, because a very high importance is then given to feeding the body alone. Beauty does not last. Form, money, and house all go. From that delusion come the sense of mine, attachment, clinging, and hatred.","To be meditating is suratva. Meditation itself is suratva. If you are meditating, you are a deva, in this sense: every sadhaka trying to know the divinity within is near the God who lives as the indweller of all. The other life is a turning away, a wandering outside. Then violence comes. Look at the world — wars, killing, the young with no direction. This generation searches outside for all its joy. A new phone every year, and joy expected from the smartphone, as if the world arrived with it.","These days ask a fast of the mind: thoughts set down, outer silence and inner silence, so that energy is conserved. A fast from social media, from Instagram, from the reels. Time disappears into them. They are addictions, and they take us far from ourselves. Whatever creates that distance is to be recognized, and the move back made at once. If the habit is three meals, let it be two. If it is already two, let it be one, ekabhukta, and even that meal very small. Malls, films, and outings are not forbidden for the rest of life. During these nine days the time is to be used.","The internal blocks are to be told to the Mother. These should leave me. They are hard, and I want to cross them. On the first day a piece of work was given: write three goals. Energy has to be given a direction, or it is misused. The purpose itself — the aim of a life, the plan with which the soul came — becomes clear only after some practice. Until then, goals are still to be set. These first three days are Ichcha Shakti. The resolves have to be the right ones. Tell her. Write it clearly. This is my desire."]$d3ens6json$::jsonb,
