insert into public.sections (id, day_id, section_order, title, content, minutes)
select
  '4b71366a-3884-42b3-ae5d-7804c1974b61'::uuid,
  d.id,
  7,
  $d3ens7title$What Do You Want · Lahiri Mahasaya$d3ens7title$,
  $d3ens7json$["Lahiri Mahasaya had one desire left, from earlier births: to live in a royal palace. Born as Lahiri, he did his work, and he did not neglect the dharma of that employment. When the work took him to Ranikhet and a little free time appeared, he felt he should climb the mountain. Near a cave a man was waiting. Have you recognized me? I am meeting you for the first time; I do not remember. The man was a guru, and he had been waiting. I have been here more than fifty years, he said — a guru waiting through a hundred and fifty years. Some of your things are here. My things are at home, Lahiri answered. Not these. Inside, the yogi showed him a kamandalu, the water-pot, the seat he used to sit on, and the darbha grass. A memory stirred, and still was not fully known. Without meditation, such a thing is not known.","Mahavatar Babaji had seen what remained. That single wish was what stopped the disciple. He was already a knower of Brahman, already at the height of knowledge of the Self. One step more, if the desire were fulfilled. This is what gurus do, and what Devi the Mother does. Whatever blocks the journey, they remove, so that the journey can be smooth — especially where the desire is the welfare of the world, the wish that this knowledge should reach everyone. Babaji created a palace and fulfilled the desire for twenty-four hours. The cave is still there. People go to it, at Ranikhet in northern India, and behind it, it is said, the palace was brought into being. For those twenty-four hours Lahiri stayed content. The desire was finished.","Ichcha Shakti puts a question many people never ask. What do you want? From childhood, no one has asked us what we really want. According to where the soul's unfolding has reached, the answer comes from inside. We do know. Clarity is the missing piece. And if the wish stands in line with the higher purpose, this power makes it manifest and complete. This is the truth. Some wishes belong to life here. Some belong to liberation: enlightenment, the light of divine knowledge, the opening of the third eye, a meeting with the gurus who abide in the great causal body.","Underneath a wish, what is actually needed may be something else, and that is what has to be caught. Suppose the wish is money. Debts, loans that cannot be repaid, calls that arrive during meditation, the electricity bill, the phone bill, taxes, the cost of a family. Suppose the money then came, completely. How would you feel? When I get what I want, what do I feel? Ask it several times. The real need may not be the first answer. He asked someone on the Zoom to try it aloud, so that everyone could see the process. Harika chose Jameela."]$d3ens7json$::jsonb,
