insert into public.sections (id, day_id, section_order, title, content, minutes)
select
  'c0006113-c7b2-410a-ae2a-3bee1dcf37a9'::uuid,
  d.id,
  8,
  $d3ens8title$Jameela · The Desire Under the Desire$d3ens8title$,
  $d3ens8json$["Jameela's wish was that her husband, a man with his doctorate, his NET and his SLET, should at last have a good and high position. If he were settled, if the family were settled, she herself could grow spiritually. If that came about, what would she feel? Contentment of the soul, atma-tripti. That would be enough. While she served for the welfare of the world, nature itself, she believed, would see to the children. He took the next step. Suppose that contentment has fully come, the children are well, and you are able to do the spiritual work. What then? She would be ready for whatever the masters would have her do. She would surrender. That, he said, is the purpose for which a person is born. Fulfil it, and the feeling is the same contentment, more fully. She went carefully toward the large words, liberation, birth and death. As long as desires remain, we keep coming and going. A mind brought to quiet. Because this birth has been taken, there are responsibilities. Whatever nature gives today — planting a tree, feeding people, teaching a meditation — doing that with the whole heart is the plan. Done that way, contentment arises, and the joy of the soul.","So the wish to place before Adi Shakti is, in truth, the wish to be content. If she is, the spiritual life goes on, the children do what is theirs, the husband is well, and because a fine vibration also comes from her, he may come to meditate. That cannot be known ahead. She added that the whole family already meditates, and that she had come to meditation through her husband. They lean on their own Shakti. Settled a little better, larger work could be done: ordinary happiness, spiritual growth, and along the way ten people helped to grow. Lakshmi, he said, stays near people of that kind, and from such a life many works can be done that hold the world up. The sankalpa was contentment in abundance, the financial difficulty cleared, and the money used so that good comes to everyone. She was saying it to her own Shakti. Mother means that power.","The question is to be asked three or four times. What do I really want? If I came out of this outer difficulty, how would I feel? Suppose the answer is peace. If peace were complete, what then? Joy. If joy came, I would want to share it. If I have shared it, what feeling is that? At the level of the Self it becomes clear what you are actually looking for. The same ladder, with a family conflict. If the tangle is resolved, peace of mind. If peace of mind, more meditation. If more meditation, I am able to be with myself. If I am with myself, the joy of the Self, and knowledge of the Self. If that knowledge has come, fulfilment, fullness. And if a sense of incompleteness comes, what is that feeling? Ask. Outside, one thing is being wished. Inside, the goal is another. On this third day, two desires or three are to be found and placed near the Mother. She will see to them.","Ichcha Shakti takes the hard places away. That power, it is said, can grind down even a mountain. Near Lalita there is a great army. Varahi is there. A minister is there, Raja Shyamala. Around Adi Shakti, many forms, divine forces with different names. The names do not have to be known. It is said she can make a mute person into a great musician. She wrote upon the tongue of an innocent man who knew nothing, and made a master: Kalidasa, Tenali Ramalinga. There was the vision of Kalika. If she wills a thing, nothing impossible is left standing."]$d3ens8json$::jsonb,
