insert into public.sections (id, day_id, section_order, title, content, minutes)
select
  'd3d7a3f3-457c-49d7-a4af-cd74d3b15914'::uuid,
  d.id,
  10,
  $d3ens10title$Shailaja and Nagaveni · Not Punishment, Training$d3ens10title$,
  $d3ens10json$["Shailaja's mind had been badly entangled. A property going back forty-three years, forty-five, was still unsettled. They are five doctors. They want the money for the welfare of the world, and the property is tangled in every direction. Everyone in the family is already in practice. Only if a real sum comes free can it be used, and it is not coming. Her wish, together with the money, is the world's good: peace, the practice toward liberation, service of the nation. It is her grandparents' property. It should be set right, and it should go to that welfare. They are five sisters. If they stand as one, a path should appear. She was writing it as he had taught: abundance, peace, liberation, and every person in the house. She placed it at Devi's feet.","She had been trying for a long time. What is not in our hands, he said, the beings of the higher worlds can solve. Divine powers resolve such things in a moment. What she herself had to do, she should do: these nine days of sadhana, done well. If it were possible, three sittings, three hours of meditation, in silence, feeling that Presence more. This had been said the day before. Devi's presence is to be felt continuously, and the wish then offered. She had already said it to the universe. Now she had said it to Prakriti. It would reach. Things would come into alignment.","Nagaveni would share tomorrow the change that had come since she learned meditation, and she would ask her questions then. What she wanted to say now was about the demonstration. Before this knowledge, if a question was invited, her hand went up: ask me, ask me. Today that had not arisen. Whoever is meant to receive a thing, receives it, at the time the universe and the gurus give it. No excitement and no anxiety had shown themselves. She thanked him for that state of mind.","Her question: we have learned that karma is training, not punishment. After a certain age, and after meditation, we can see that a trouble arrived so something might be learned. Children, and all of us before meditation, have no such seeing. Chronic illness comes, and the child does not know, I brought this. Does it not then become punishment?","Until eighteen, children live under their parents' protection, inside their energy field. The first three years are the mother's care. Then the father draws the child close, girl or boy, and holds the child. From the first school, from LKG, the protection of teachers comes in. Learning begins with mother, then father, then guru, and continues until eighteen. After the menstrual cycle begins, a girl comes more fully into the mother's care. A boy goes toward the father. With a masculine energy, the father teaches how outer challenges are met. That energy helps. A girl remains with the mother.","A child of five with a chronic illness knows nothing of karma or rebirth, and cannot yet practise. Because the child is inside the parents' care, their part is very large. If illness expresses itself through the children, the parents carry the responsibility until the problem is solved. An autistic child needs a great deal of unconditional love, cannot communicate, is sometimes hyperactive and sometimes shouting. The love is given without anger. If the parents are living a meditation, the children learn by seeing. They mimic: I will sit as mother sits. Force them, and they stiffen and will not. Children are never to be forced. The adult becomes the example.","In the universe there is no punishment, only training: lessons of the soul. A cold teaches. A fever teaches. Eating, even without hunger, from a want that rose inside — junk food, pizza, pasta — and an upset stomach: that too is a lesson, and the next time only the food that keeps the body comfortable is taken. Parents can convey this as a seed. The child catches the point. Children cannot solve it alone.","Most often it is a karmic situation shared with the parents. A son is angry with his father from the beginning, speaks well with his mother, rejects whatever the father says. The child cannot yet see why. The father, meditating daily, can. In that other birth we were enemy kings. A conflict was never resolved. Unfinished business. Now he is born as my son, and the enmity is still there. The father receives the lesson himself. No judgment, no criticism: acceptance, and love. When he does that, it resolves. The bond is runanubandha, karmic debt. In meditation the parent comes to know what this boy or this girl needs, and that if the help is given through him, they come out of it. At the level of the soul we plan a life and then arrive. The lessons are compulsory. That compulsory learning is the training. Even in childhood, the offering can be made in this way."]$d3ens10json$::jsonb,
