insert into public.sections (id, day_id, section_order, title, content, minutes)
select
  '84eb3f07-8b9c-42ac-ae4d-0b171a27e17a'::uuid,
  d.id,
  11,
  $d3ens11title$Co-Created Reality · The Song in the Heart$d3ens11title$,
  $d3ens11json$["Nagaveni had watched a film a couple of days before. She spoke of it as a film of Hanuman's amsha, a portion of Hanuman. People who do not meditate like such a film, she said, because it shows a power beyond the senses, and it pleases them to think that gods have power of that kind. In it a swami opens the lock of a prison. Food in his hand multiplies many times over. During the British time, sadhakas of this kind were here. They know beforehand. Why did they not stop what was coming? So many heroes were going to die.","Some realities are co-created. Many people together keep creating them. The British made this country a slave country and wielded their power. That was against free will. They killed many heroes. It was inhuman. At Jallianwala Bagh they fired as if shooting birds. Even now it boils in us; those who died are our brothers and sisters. A massacre was done. And the events sit inside a reality that was made together.","If a guru wished, a snap of the fingers and it would be over. If Krishna snapped his fingers, it would be over, and then there would be no play. Every soul has to come to that level by going through what is there to go through. There is no shortcut. The British too could have been handed enlightenment long ago. Himalayan gurus are many, gurus like Neem Karoli Baba. A snap of the fingers would do it. It is otherwise, because every soul and every soul's plan is to be respected. Only for some, and only in such a presence, is there an intervention. A life that is ending may be lengthened by forty years, because by remaining in that body the person does a great good for the world. In a co-created reality they do not interfere. A dissolution comes, a flood, a storm, an earthquake, and they do not stop it. They know a hundred thousand will die. Each soul, in its evolution, has experiences it must pass through.","They see with the vision of the Self, and so they can accept every thing. They do not sort the world into right and wrong. They are beyond right and wrong, beyond victim and perpetrator, beyond plus and minus. The defect of sattva is that we get stuck there, judging. They are past that. We too have seen this film, he said. It has been made wonderfully: the life of Neem Karoli Baba. Every sadhaka should see it. From childhood he was in practice. Without the seeds of many births, a child does not sit like that, always in meditation, with none of the ordinary playing and wanting. Rama, continuously. Such people were yogis through many births, and are born again with a purpose.","Through Harika, each of these days, a song of the Mother is heard, and heard in that way it remains in the heart. Her melody is something expressed out of knowledge of the Self, and what is expressed from there does a great deal of good. She sang. The hymn opens on the Mother as Omkara rupini, she whose form is Om. When the song ended he said it was wonderful. Tomorrow, again, in Jnanodayam."]$d3ens11json$::jsonb,
