insert into public.sections (id, day_id, section_order, title, content, minutes)
select
  '2f9a2c71-e0dc-41f9-a0e3-0ae4cd6463e8'::uuid,
  d.id,
  4,
  $d4ens4title$The Pond and the Five Fires · Maya and the Senses$d4ens4title$,
  $d4ens4json$["These are fierce wants of the aihika kind. Aihika means here: this gross world of things, and the thought that never stops saying I want this and I want that. When do such thoughts grow less? Rambha was made of them. That is why the name is his. He did his tapas inside a pond, staying in the water to meditate. Meditation can be done at ease, in a kindly place. Why enter the water? This, too, is a symbol.","The water may be taken as emotion. What we expected does not happen, and we are upset: a work left undone today, a hope that never came, a desire that failed. In this gross world things do not happen as they were pictured. It did not happen — why did it not happen? Worry crowds in. Anger comes, and sorrow. If someone has rejected us, the descent can reach depression: I will do nothing, I will sit in the house. In the symbol, this is the life of our passions.","There is another reading. A phone falls from a boat into the river. It is down there, and it cannot be seen. On dry ground a lost thing can be found by lifting what covers it. In water it sinks and stays hidden. Those who study the ocean are searching what the seas contain. The womb of the sea holds many secrets. From outside there is only water. Go inside, and what is there becomes known.","The water is also a sign of maya. Rambha did his tapas while remaining in it. This world of maya feels as though it were the truth, and it is not. It keeps feeling as though other people were the cause of one's sorrow. In Rambha's condition, we live inside that maya. Yet the tapas is for mukti, the longing to be free. He too wants enlightenment, a release from this one day. We are stuck, and everything around us is an entanglement, and still the final goal has to be enlightenment. People say that problems are chasing them, that so many are hurting them, that others or the circumstances are the reason for their pain. Believed in that way, the pain increases. Why did they speak like that yesterday? Why are they looking at me like this? Why those words? No one is the cause of our sorrow. Rambha's condition is one in which tamas is the larger part: laziness, a dullness of mind. He cannot see past it. He looks at the world of things and says that these objects, this situation, produced my sorrow.","We ourselves are the cause of our sorrow. The cause is our ignorance, our avidya. Where true knowledge is absent, every small thing hurts us. The account says Rambha meditated in the pond, and Karambha under a banyan, among the five fires. They were brothers. They could have sat side by side and practised in comfort. That one of them practised in the open, under the banyan, among the five fires, is Vedavyasa Maharshi giving a sign.","Prakriti, nature, is the form of maya, because it is made of the three gunas. What is not appears as though it were. What is appears as though it were not. What truly is never appears as it is. Vemana's line says that the one who conquers maya is the yogi who knows the secret. The yogi has to know it by experience. Karambha is practising there, among the five fires, under the banyan. Those five fires of nature are to be known as our five jnanendriyas, the organs of knowledge. He is in the middle of them, touching and yet not clinging. Eyes, ears, nose, tongue, and skin carry us outward without a break, and so does the mind, another and a chief organ.","Karambha's condition is this: I must attain the knowledge of moksha, I must know myself. He practised in earnest. Yogis do in fact sit amid five fires. A severe heat is borne, the sun overhead, the body burning, and they do not move. They put the body through great difficulty. Taken as a symbol, those same fires are the five organs of knowledge. They pull. The pull has to be withdrawn, and the face turned inward. That is what is said of Karambha. He is an asura. Tamas and rajas are the greater share, and sattva is also present. He has not yet become aware inside this maya. He is practising while maya itself is still unrecognized."]$d4ens4json$::jsonb,
