insert into public.sections (id, day_id, section_order, title, content, minutes)
select
  'ace51074-90d9-4f0e-a5bd-a54932eebae0'::uuid,
  d.id,
  6,
  $d4ens6title$The Offered Head · Putra and the Twice-Born$d4ens6title$,
  $d4ens6json$["They were elder and younger. When Indra had killed the brother, Karambha began a practice still more severe. He offered his own head into one of the five fires. He cut it away and surrendered it. A tapas of that severity is itself a symbol. He had seen Rambha caught in the mind, and the younger brother's practice stopped. He would not become like that. The head, here, is the mind. Karambha surrendered it to the fire and merged it there. To merge the mind into the Atman: that is the meaning. Fire stands for the tattva of Paramatman, the tattva of the Atman. Then Agni appeared and said, ask for a boon. A wish was already there. Karambha asked for a son of great strength. This, too, is a symbol.","Agni means truth, and truth is the Atman: satya, eternal, ancient, permanent, the tattva of Paramatman. In the form of fire the Vedas and the Upanishads have always spoken of it. What is it like? The Katha Upanishad says: anor aniyan mahato mahiyan — smaller than the atom, subtler than the subtle, and greater than the great. By the measure of our science, he said, this universe has spread across some ninety-six billion light years. How many such universes are there? How vast is even this one? Greater than the great: that is said of the field of the Atman.","The word putra is a symbol in the same way. A saying, a sukti, and a verse say that the son saves one from the hell called Put. Put means that hell. Tra means that which protects. In India this was read as a demand for a male child only. If a daughter was born, people grieved. From that reading came female foeticide: scans and ultrasound, and if the child is a girl, an abortion. It is a great sin. Vedavyasa's symbol was taken wrongly. A girl comes as Lakshmi. A girl is the form of Lakshmi Mata, of Durga Mata, of Saraswati Mata.","In the real sense of the text, putra is the new you that arises from you, the new birth you take from yourself. A knower of the Self is called a dvija, twice-born, born a second time in this same life: once before meditation, and once after. If the knowledge of the practice has been done, you are born again as a new knower of the Self. Before meditation, life is one story. Practise, and you come to know a great deal about yourself. Every petal of the flower of Self-knowledge opens. After meditation, the story is another.","This is why the books of India can be misread. The line about the hell called Put has been followed by many terrible things. The real meaning is punah, again: hell as repeated birth. The cycles of birth and death are the actual hell. Thousands of crores of times we keep coming. An old reckoning says we entered eighty-six lakhs of yonis before we came to this earth. It is a symbol, a number: subtle living things, animals, many beings, and at last a human birth. Even then, six hundred to eight hundred human births, many of them wasted, and some people take still more. It is beyond counting. Eighty-six lakhs of lifetimes: from the mineral kingdom we became plants, from plants animals, cruel beasts and then gentle animals, and then human. Inside the human birth itself there are many stages. Many of those births are wasted.","Putra, in this meaning, is the one who can cross birth and death. Thirst and unfinished business, held in ignorance, become the cause of another life. Projects are taken up and left pending. Each birth offers certain experiences. We arrive having decided what this life is for, and then we postpone. The birth is wasted.","Many people were not born merely in order to survive, or for a nine-to-five post. They have already done a great deal of meditation, and they were born for another purpose. After some practice the job no longer resonates. They decide to live this spiritual life completely, through the whole day.","After my medical studies were finished, not for a moment did I feel I should remain there. Medicine is a great science. The science of the spirit is higher. I did not feel this birth should be wasted. Money can be earned, a hospital built, many surgeries done. That was not the purpose. A birth is taken for a reason, and it has to be tuned to that purpose. What we were born to do has to be done. Otherwise the dissatisfaction remains inside."]$d4ens6json$::jsonb,
  7
