insert into public.sections (id, day_id, section_order, title, content, minutes)
select
  'a042ac32-cd6d-4e9d-aec9-f1c6e4ecbfd9'::uuid,
  d.id,
  9,
  $d4ens9title$No Enemy Outside · The Mother Who Is Waiting$d4ens9title$,
  $d4ens9json$["In these days of Devi Navaratri the first work is to face our inner enemies. Outside, there are no enemies. Husband, wife, children, circumstances: none of these is the cause of my sorrow. The cause is our ignorance, the absence of a complete knowledge of ourselves. An interpretation is already loaded in the mind. Through that limited knowledge, from that angle and through that lens, the world appears. This world of maya, seen in that way, is the state of Rambha.","He is stuck in maya, and the asura qualities are with him. Karambha is doing his practice, and the asura qualities are still there. From the hell called Put, from these cycles of birth and death, he came forward doing sadhana, wishing to come out. These Navaratri days are also days in which we recognize many things inside ourselves. A state like Rambha's has come in us as well. Once, I had it. You have had it. Everyone keeps having it.","The world of things, the world of maya, keeps pulling us outward. Outward, and outward again, we try to run. These nine days are for going inward. We have to go near Amma. Amma means Shakti, the Mother who is herself the form of that power. Amma is present in us as Kundalini Shakti, and she is waiting. She is waiting for the day we close our eyes and meditate. Will it be done with the eyes closed? She waits. Amma is hidden, and she is asleep, and she is waiting for you. For how long she has been waiting. We have to go near Amma. Then that Kundalini Shakti wakes. She moves upward. Whatever goals are set, they come to be fulfilled. And still, we have to come out from under the great thief called the mind. That great thief has to be caught.","In here, there is an inner purification. These inner enemies have to be conquered. That conquest is Mahishasura-mardini: Sridevi, the Mother who slew Mahishasura. Today the telling has come as far as Rambha and Karambha. After this, Mahishasura himself, and how his arising happened, will also be known. A boon was given to Karambha. At this point in the story a pause is kept. There is no stop here that would finish it. Tomorrow it continues. Karambha asks for the boon, and according to the boon something is given. What boon did he ask? And after that, how was Mahishasura born? Why, when the father was in a human body, was the son born with the body of a buffalo? Mahisha means a male buffalo. Why did Vedavyasa convey it in that symbol? What knowledge does Mahishasura give us? We are not to become like Mahishasura. How does Devi Mata slay him? Inside us, too, there is a Mahishasura. Rambha is there. Karambha is there. Mahishasura is there as well.","That, too, we will come to know. He turned, then, to a story told as a sign of the same work."]$d4ens9json$::jsonb,
  5
