insert into public.sections (id, day_id, section_order, title, content, minutes)
select
  '815334d1-e724-44f3-a3aa-cb5d07052e0f'::uuid,
  d.id,
  11,
  $d4ens11title$Elephant and Mosquito · The Practice for Today$d4ens11title$,
  $d4ens11json$["Once an elephant was standing under a tree. It was a large elephant, a very large one. A mosquito came there. The mosquito settled on the elephant and took its rest. After a while it prepared to leave, to go from that tree to another place. At that time the mosquito woke from its rest, and it spoke. O Elephant, sir, thank you, thank you, thank you. Resting on you, I also gave you my weight. I gave you too much weight. Because of me you must have felt a great weight. I am sorry. I ask your pardon. I have troubled you.","The elephant's answer was this. I did not even know that you were there. I did not know that you had landed on me, or that you had any weight. These mosquitoes, he said, are the problems in our life. We are people of an elephant's size. Our Atman is the great elephant: magnificent, exalted, strong, of great power. The Atman has all of these qualities. Are we going to live in the state of the mosquito, or in the state of the elephant? That is the decision we have to make. Problems come, and problems go. The mosquito comes, and the mosquito leaves. The mind, though, arrives. The mosquito has landed on me. The mosquito has bitten me. Thinking about it, meditating upon it, we waste the time.","Friends, the points learned in today's class are today's practice. No one is the cause of our sorrow. We ourselves are the makers of our joy. Rambha and Karambha, samsara and nirvana: both are important, first. Afterwards, one of them drops, of itself. Rambha drops. Our samsara, slowly, slowly, becomes something we can live as a drop of water on a lotus leaf. We learn that living through the practice. Nothing is to be abandoned. We have to come into tune with whatever we were born for.","There was another class waiting, and so this morning's class was brought to a close a little early. Harika would speak with people after the class. Before that, one act of offering was still to be done."]$d4ens11json$::jsonb,
