insert into public.sections (id, day_id, section_order, title, content, minutes)
select
  'e6457d8a-650a-4fae-a951-101f89783bfa'::uuid,
  d.id,
  1,
  $d5ens1title$Opening Meditation · Sahasrara Pyramid$d5ens1title$,
  $d5ens1json$["Welcome to the 565th day of the Jnanodayam programme conducted by Quantum Life University. We are on the fifth day of Navaratri, learning from Dr. Newton Kondaveti what Devi means, what the Mother means, and how a human being surrenders — with practicals and with processes. Before that knowledge is received, we sit as we did yesterday. The practice is Anapanasati, mindfulness of the natural breath.","Sit in sukhasana, on a chair or on a mat. On a chair the feet may be crossed. Close the eyes, and with a small smile observe the breath. It is already happening. Nothing is to be controlled or held. Noticing it as it is is the whole work. Continue for another twenty minutes.","Stay with the breath. In the last ten minutes, turn toward the welfare of the world and carry the energy to the Sahasrara Pyramid, meant to serve everyone. With the divine eye, see it: a temple of knowledge, energy coming from the divine realm toward this earth. This age needs peace, self-knowledge, maitri, and karuna. Through the pyramid these are to be awakened in everyone, at the highest level.","With the sankalpa that the self-knowledge in each person should wake, let us become partners in this creation. Feel that we are seated around the pyramid. By the common resolve and the sense of oneness, the building proceeds. People changed by it come from the four corners of the world, practise, and attain self-knowledge. For some hundreds of years it is to serve, and that we may be partners is our fortune. Let it be completed soon, in the right way, the right people and the resources gathering without strain. On the 24th of November, 2027, we see ourselves seated inside it and meditating, the inauguration held with Dr. Newton and Dr. Lakshmi.","With the faith that the universe itself brings this about in the right manner, release the sankalpa, and return to the breath. The last two minutes are simply the breath, slowing, aware. In the last minute: five, four, three, two, one, zero. Place both hands over the eyes for a few moments, and open the eyes with a small smile.","The fifth day is given in person by Brahmarshi Chakravarti Dr. Newton Kondaveti, who shows what a true celebration is. Cameras on, and with a smile we welcome him. Thank you, Sir. Over to you. Thank you, Harika madam. Good morning, dear friends. Jnanodayam. Devi Navaratri we dedicate specially for sadhana."]$d5ens1json$::jsonb,
  4
