insert into public.sections (id, day_id, section_order, title, content, minutes)
select
  'f0d0da7c-edb6-495c-ad3a-cd0ff4fc35bd'::uuid,
  d.id,
  2,
  $d5ens2title$Two Navaratris · Aham and Sarvam$d5ens2title$,
  $d5ens2json$["Every day we are learning many things, and the special nature of this festival, from the spiritual side. Navaratri comes twice. The Navaratri that comes with Ramanavami is Chaitra Navaratri. The one we are in now is Ashwayuja Navaratri, falling in this season, around September and October. Both have a very special place in India. Of the Navaratri observed in April, at the time of Sri Ramanavami, a story is told: how Sri Rama, after the slaying of Ravana, celebrated Vijayotsava, and how he took part in those Devi Navaratri days.","Chaitra Navaratri was established for the sadhana of Aham Brahmasmi — ‘I am Brahman.’ Our rishis and yogis celebrate those spring nights in order to know that state. Sadhana is done then. The meaning is this. Whichever god I am searching for, whichever Brahman, whichever Krishna, whichever Vishnu — whatever I am searching for — that itself is me. To know this is the first step.","The speciality of the Navaratri that comes in Ashwayuja is different, and it is twin to the first. These nights are for knowing, by direct experience, Sarvam khalvidam Brahma — ‘All this, verily, is Brahman.’ Both are important. They are twin aspects. If a person knows only Aham Brahmasmi, a spiritual ego can arise. I am God; everyone else is a demon; everyone else is ignorant; I am the very form of knowledge — and the rest are looked down upon as ignorant. That is not enough. That is not knowledge. It is not pure knowledge.","Sarvam khalvidam Brahma says: as I am, so is everyone. The sorrow I undergo, everyone undergoes. Like me, everyone is striving for mukti, for moksha, for enlightenment, for jnanodayam — the dawn of knowledge. Everyone wants to be free of sorrow. The divinity in me is in everyone. All the nature we see is filled with Paramatma, the Supreme. Otherwise a notion remains: this nature is one thing, and Paramatma is something else.","From that split, destruction follows. For his own gains man cuts trees, forests perish, and hills are torn open for gold, diamonds, or copper. River waters are polluted for a small profit, because Sarvam khalvidam Brahma is not known. This nature itself is Paramatma. The trees are gods. The hill is God. Stones and rocks are divine forms. In every atom, in every particle, he is there. Hiranyakashipu asked Prahlada where this Vishnu was, this Narayana. Prahlada answered: everywhere — in the atom, in the particle, wherever one looks.","Prahlada’s state is Sarvam khalvidam Brahma. He had already attained Aham Brahmasmi, and this as well. The Navaratri we are in now is for this second sadhana. Every kingdom of nature is included: mineral, plant, animal, human, deva, yaksha, kinnara, gandharva, and the angelic kingdom. All are part of this nature, filled with divinity and shining with it. Yogis and rishis prescribed the sadhana. They did not set it down casually."]$d5ens2json$::jsonb,
