insert into public.sections (id, day_id, section_order, title, content, minutes)
select
  '795c5e87-09c1-49b0-a970-c2e206947a0a'::uuid,
  d.id,
  4,
  $d5ens4title$Contentment · The Zero State$d5ens4title$,
  $d5ens4json$["Paramahamsa Yogananda used to give this statement. In the material world, in the wheel of samsara, we should live with contentment. Be content with what is. Do not scramble after what is not there. A disciple once came to a guru with the question everyone carries: how is ananda to be gained? We are all searching only for joy. We want to abide in joy. One day there is joy; the next day depression, sorrow, pain. These swings come. We call them mood swings. We travel from this side to that. There is no single step that stays, nothing that is permanent.","The guru did not answer at once. He asked the disciple: if something precious is with you, how do you feel? Very good — joy. If you lose it? Pain comes. If you gain it back? Joy returns. Then the guru said: see to it that whatever you have remains with you, in you. Contentment will come. Joy will come. Do not scramble after what you do not have.","‘I don’t have this, I don’t have this’ — that itself is the cause of sorrow. That creates the sorrow. ‘I don’t have this; I want that; I want that.’ This is why material contentment is paired with spiritual discontent. On the spiritual side a certain discontent should always remain. Otherwise ego arrives. It can arrive at any time. It is like a game in which the snake may swallow us at any moment. The moment we think, I have come to know everything, our story is finished. Our own ego is what brings the fall. We should always remain in the zero state.","Rambha has many material desires, and he is making an effort toward sadhana, but he is stuck in maya. This is a maya-world; the whole of this is a maya-world. Here addictions crowd in. Everything becomes an addiction. We talk about the outer ones we know — alcohol, smoking — but there is also approval addiction. Everyone’s approval must be won. Everyone’s praise must be had. Everyone should support me. They should say that I am great. Many people are addicted to approval. There is relationship addiction too: the bond with other people is needed; I must have the tie. We get bound. When do bonds bind? Only atma-bandha, the bond of the Self, brings us out. It is a bond that is not a bond.","After coming onto the path of meditation we regard one another as atma-bandhus, kin of the Self. That is all. It does not bind. Souls living in bodies — nothing here is permanent — and we hold that awareness, that consciousness, that prajna. Through that alone, continuously, like Karambha, the attention stays there, on one main goal above the rest: moksha-jnana, enlightenment, atma-jnana, Brahma-jnana. Remaining in the zero state, we practise and we continue, because there are many steps. The infinite that has to be known keeps being known. Humility is required. Vinaya is required.","Taken in essence, Rambha is destroyed first. The sadhaka overcomes him. The material desires that were pulling and pressing are dissolved into Paramatma, and clarity about the goal comes. Karambha grows alert: am I caught in this? The old woman will seize me and I will perish. Sadhana has to continue carefully, amid the five fires. The two in us have to be balanced, and the first rule is not to suppress. Material desires are not crushed. As knowledge grows they slip away, one by one.","There is nothing in the outer stuff. We will not carry even one paisa. What comes with us is the dharma we have done, the knowledge we have gathered, and our experiences — inner experiences, meditation experiences. That knowledge, that sadhana, is what we carry. When sadhakas realise this, Rambha departs and Karambha practises more carefully. The cycles of birth and death are not a place to get stuck. They have to be crossed. That is the sadhana Karambha did. Amid the five fires he severed his own head and offered it to Agni: he offered everything in him, all the desires. Caught by desire, destroyed by the old woman, the sadhana stopped, pain came, and then it was begun again. Karambha continued. The two brothers are two states in the jivatma. From the Karambha-state, the Mahisha-state comes."]$d5ens4json$::jsonb,
