insert into public.sections (id, day_id, section_order, title, content, minutes)
select
  '8a2091d6-5a3b-44bb-a75d-10aaa9d1ea46'::uuid,
  d.id,
  7,
  $d5ens7title$Inner Enemies · Three Living Pictures$d5ens7title$,
  $d5ens7json$["Bhashpala is kama, and a person has many desires, not one. A merchant had a house. In the next town he saw a palace and resolved to build one like it. Beyond what he had, he took every kind of debt, raised the palace, and in the end sold all his properties. Desire mixed with greed remained only as tears, as bhashpa. Unovercome, this enemy keeps us weeping. Devi Shakti is what makes the conquest.","Durmukha is anger. A sculptor in a village had wonderful skill, and anger at everything. He does not see his own face. He looks at others and thinks he is fine. He carved a splendid image of a deity, and one finger came out a little crooked. Anger rose until he smashed the image he himself had made. Anger toward others is one thing. Anger toward oneself is self-sabotage, stabbing oneself with that knife. As a mere story, none of this appears.","Tamra is lobha. A rich man loved gold as his life, piled the house with ornaments and coins, and spent nothing. Greed hides: bank accounts, black money, a bank somewhere far off. He hesitated even to eat well. Except how to conceal the wealth — thieves might come; income tax might take it — there was no other thought. One night the thieves carried the hoard away, and he became a beggar. The money had left neither comfort nor peace. It went like rosewater poured into ashes. A master is generous, in the knowledge given and in conduct. If we hide, we are robbed. If we share, we are increased.","Chichchura is moha, present without our knowing. Duryodhana’s parents had it, gave the wrong guidance, and he went the wrong way. A tender plant not bent while small will not bend as a tree. Meditation has to be taught first. A child should hear that self-knowledge exists. What is said instead is: become an engineer, a doctor, study, earn, become a magnate — speech about what perishes and what brings sorrow. That moha binds the children, and they live in ignorance. Earning need not be refused. A good doctor, a good engineer — but the foundation first, and meditation is the foundation. Upanayana was established for this. Even in childhood, Aham Brahmasmi and Tat Tvam Asi: you are not this, dear one; you are That. Said again and again, it still has to come down into practice.","Asiloma is pride. Ego makes us fall, and to break it the universe itself sends lessons. If wrong is done in ego, nature does not stay quiet. An illness comes, and the head has to bow. Cancer comes. This is not to say that everyone with cancer is an egotist. Causes differ, and much is not in our hands. What ego produces is ‘I alone am great.’ The more we learn, the more humbly we can abide.","Bidala is matsarya. A husband meditating well was told by the divine power to ask a boon, on one condition: whatever you ask, double of it goes to your wife. He asked for jewels, for gold, and the double came to her. The second boon was a great deal of money, and again the double came to her. At the third, a murderous jealousy rose. Give me a small heart attack — not so as to die. That much envy can sit in us without our knowing.","The embassy failed. The six were slain, and the arishadvargas were crossed. Mada remained in Mahishasura: ahankara, and the intense subtle ego. Those who do this sadhana get ego more than others. The subtle, and the ego subtler than the subtle, has to be cut as well. Devi Shakti destroyed that too, and slew Mahishasura. While we practise, a great awareness has to be kept. The state to remain in is ‘I do not know’ — what has been known is a grain of sand, and what is still to be known is a mountain. Learning continues in that humility. Thanks are due to Vedavyasa. He gave us the Devi Bhagavatam, and through these stories set the secrets of yoga and of meditation in our hands, so that we may attain Sarvam khalvidam Brahma. This entire nature is that Paramatma-principle."]$d5ens7json$::jsonb,
