insert into public.sections (id, day_id, section_order, title, content, minutes)
select
  '7f5897c2-bc7c-44e1-a39d-8da59ba9c5f1'::uuid,
  d.id,
  8,
  $d5ens8title$Equal Vision · Jivanmukti$d5ens8title$,
  $d5ens8json$["Today let us mark the practice as well. However we look, the seeing should be like this. Whatever tree we see, a devata should appear there. The Lord himself should appear. Paramatma has appeared in that tree. A mango tree is seen — an ordinary tree — and a devata has appeared. To Gomata, the mother cow, a devata has appeared. To a dog, a devata. Animals, birds, whatever appears: an ant appears, and the ant is the devata. A mosquito appears, and it is the devata. The whole of nature as divine form — that is the vision we need. Sarvam khalvidam. Whomever we see.","In your house, in our own house, there are enemies. Even when we see the enemies in the house, we have to see this same thing inside them. They too are divine forms. They have not yet known. While they are in the state of not knowing, in ignorance, they keep creating sorrow for everyone. Everyone lives in himsa, in violence. A person in whom the eye of knowledge has come, whose buddhi has blossomed, with equal vision and equal feeling, does not judge anyone. Their time will come. They too will one day become masters. They too will do the sadhana of meditation. If not this birth, another birth. That is all.","There is no need that everything happen in this birth itself. This is a journey of many births. For some, many births are taken. In this birth seeds are planted. In another birth they sprout. There is no such rule that within another ten years, in this life, they must attain enlightenment. According to each one’s sadhana, they attain those states and that knowledge.","In today’s class we are speaking of victory over the arishadvargas, the inner enemies. The six rakshasas are the six in us: kama, krodha, lobha, moha, mada, matsarya. They have to be recognised. Has each one been recognised? Identified? Diagnosed? It is easy to think, there is nothing in me, all is well. Many people are like the ostrich, hiding the head in the sand: nothing is there, all is fine, all is fine. It should not be so. As long as we wear this physical body, some faults are also there. They have to be corrected here. In the Atman there are no faults. In the field of the Atman we are all gods: Aham Brahmasmi, Aham Shivosmi, Aham Krishnosmi. But with the delusion of the body, this personality — body, mind, chitta, buddhi, and ahankara joined together — flaws are there. Toward these we have to be vigilant. Awareness has to be there. Otherwise we get stuck, and sadhana is interrupted.","The state of jivanmukti, as Adi Shankaracharya has said: if we are to be jivanmuktas, free while living, then while we are in this body itself we must know. What has to be known must be known. The one knowledge by which all knowledges become known — that knowledge. A single point: Aham Brahmasmi, Tat Tvam Asi, Sarvam khalvidam Brahma. Aham Brahmasmi is to be known, and Sarvam khalvidam Brahma. These two. Every meditation sadhaka’s fruit is these two. They come to know them by experience."]$d5ens8json$::jsonb,
