insert into public.sections (id, day_id, section_order, title, content, minutes)
select
  'da728955-8037-4847-a30a-022531c747e0'::uuid,
  d.id,
  9,
  $d5ens9title$Devi Samarpan · The Ninefold Offering$d5ens9title$,
  $d5ens9json$["Wonderful, friends. Today let us once again do the Devi Samarpan we have been practising from the first day. Sit at ease in Lakshmi mudra. More of our attention is for the Shakti: the divine Shakti in us, Devi Shakti. She is present in us as Kundalini. We have to surrender to that Shakti. That is Devi Samarpan. That same Shakti is this entire creation. She is all of nature. Close the right nostril, and through the left nostril draw the breath inward nine times. Nine times means up to a count of nine, and not as one breath. Successive sips. This is being said for those who are new. Inhale inward nine times. If the breath is taken in a rush, by the third or the fourth you cannot inhale, because the lungs are already full. Draw it slowly, gently, nine times. Nine, to match the nine nights of Navaratri.","Then the hands come into namaskara mudra. The breath is held. With sharanu, sharanu — I take refuge — Devi Samarpan is made as a complete bowing down. One must become surrendered to the Devi Mother. The Shakti in us must be surrendered. That Shakti slays everything the six enemies are doing. She slays Mahishasura. All the bad qualities in us go. That Shakti washes them clean.","After the bow has touched, Shreem, Shreem, Shreem is repeated — at the para level, in the mind, not pronounced outwardly — nine times inside. If that bija is not to your liking, then a stream of counting: one, two, three, four, any single sequence, nine times. The count matters. Nine is matched to nine. Then you may return to the original position. Friends, this is to be done nine times.","Let us do it. Sit comfortably. Slowly let the breath go outward as the head bows. Bend the head. Then hold. Stop the breath, and within: Shreem, nine times. Slowly take the breath again and come back to your place. The feeling is what matters. With what feeling it is done — that is the important thing. Devi Samarpan is complete surrender. Become surrendered to that Shakti. To the Kundalini Shakti, to the Shakti of the universe. To the Shakti of Prakriti, the Mother. To the Shakti of Jagannmata, Mother of the world. Do it at your own pace, in your own way. The bhava is what matters.","Those who have finished the nine rounds, remain seated in silence. Sit like a statue, without fidgeting, still — an achala state. In the mind too there is no movement. No thoughts are needed. Those whose breath has settled, simply be. The others, complete the remaining rounds. The offering itself cleanses. What the six enemies do in us, the Shakti to whom we have bowed brings to an end."]$d5ens9json$::jsonb,
