insert into public.sections (id, day_id, section_order, title, content, minutes)
select
  'bdf7eac0-241d-4090-a150-c678f06a9465'::uuid,
  d.id,
  11,
  $d5ens11title$Questions · Addiction and Healing$d5ens11title$,
  $d5ens11json$["Wonderful, friends. Let us take a few sharings. Yesterday some hands were raised, and two or three of them can be given the chance. Siddu garu. Namaskaram. Thank you, Sir. Maharaj, greetings. His question: toxic people are as if intoxicated — how are such people to be handled? Should we ourselves remain in a meditative state? And a second question, from the Anastasia book. In that book the grandfather tells Anastasia that when the mother, in order to heal a woman, sends forth her own force and heals, that should not be done. That one point had raised a doubt.","Wonderful, Siddu. Very good. The first question is about addiction, about vice, about addiction to intoxicating substances. Many people fall into these addictions because of the pain in them. They are covering it. They do not know how to come out of the pain. They do not know how to come out of sorrow. For some the pain is severe. For some it has lain there from childhood. They have been carrying it from the past, from a long time back. Alcohol, or drugs, whatever is being taken, is used like a temporary pacifier. They carpet over the pain. That is all. This has to be understood. There is intense sorrow in them.","They are using this method. Addiction to intoxicants. The young generation, from childhood itself: drugs, or alcohol, or smoking. Temporarily some kind of state arises. And that too because of chemical dependence. Through those chemicals a light feeling comes. It conceals the sorrow to some extent. It hides the pain, inside. This is very dangerous. How long can it be carried? Day by day the dependence, the intoxicant, destroys the body completely. It destroys the mental system as well. Clear thinking does not come. A criminal mind sets in. When the substance is not to be had, for the sake of money they start stealing. It has to be bought, and so everything that should not be done, every adharma, gets done.","The solution is one: meditation, and counselling with it. Meditation first — even if they are asked to sit, they cannot sit. Counselling has to be given. In them there is what is called a shame-wound. There is toxic shame. Healthy shame is one thing; toxic shame is another. To cover that toxic shame they habituate themselves to alcohol and drugs. Through counselling, awareness has to be brought about in them. What painful events are in the life — unable to tell anyone, they keep them inside. They swallow everything. Many do not even know how to express it, do not know how to say it. All of this is very useful. If counselling is done first, they become able to come into meditation.","Have they meditated? Have they caught hold? For these vices, meditation is called a good addiction. A good vice: every day turning inward. It corrects us in many ways. One by one we separate what is inside, and the Shakti corrects every fault that is in us. A meditation sadhaka cannot do adharma. Corruption, any of it — he cannot. That state, that Shakti in us, creates awareness. It creates the knowledge.","The second question is healing. Healing is possible, because great masters have that power. The power to heal is in everyone. But we should not heal. Why? Each person has, in themselves, the power and the capacity to heal themselves. There are exceptions to the rule. For a rule, ninety-nine percent: he should not heal. In the one percent, if this person is of use for the uplift of the world — if a guru sees that everything obstructing him can be taken out, that he will be of use, that if he lives another fifty years then through him a great good will come to crores of people — then the guru heals him. He is the right person. The lifespan is expanded, extended. In some specific circumstances and conditions, healing is done for some people. In general, self-healing is the right method. Everyone: we have to bring health to ourselves.","Through meditation, through knowledge, and through grasping this Shakti, three things come. When the mind becomes zero, the body recuperates. Psychosomatic diseases slowly leave, and stress goes. Then the cause has to be known: why this illness is there, which conflict brought it. That knowledge comes in meditation itself, in an altered state of consciousness, and that is what heals. When the eye of knowledge opens, the karma-vasanas and the conflicts are burnt to ash. Many find that even as the third eye is opening, the old troubles shatter — finished, the shop closed. If it has opened, the goal is as good as struck. Prarabdha karma and sanchita karma go. Swasthata, health, follows swasthiti, one’s own natural state. Know that state, and health comes.","So Anastasia: she has the capacity to heal, and healing is done. But a guru considers to whom it should be done. Suppose someone is healed, and afterwards he commits a hundred murders. We heal a person, and he goes and does a hundred murders, and many corruptions, many scandals. That papa we would be taking on. This is why, whoever comes to us, the first word is: dear one, do meditation. Attain awareness. Find out why this came in you. This illness, these diseases, are also indirect teachers — paroksha gurus. There is something you have to learn from that teacher. Therefore the illness came. Know what it is. If they do the sadhana, they will certainly attain it. Siddu garu asked a good question. Thank you."]$d5ens11json$::jsonb,
  9
