insert into public.sections (id, day_id, section_order, title, content, minutes)
select
  'c95ce779-976a-4e52-aea4-55777cab6ffc'::uuid,
  d.id,
  12,
  $d5ens12title$Sharings · Tithi and Tomorrow$d5ens12title$,
  $d5ens12json$["Kalpana garu, and then Kavita garu, had raised a hand the day before. Through Jnanodayam a great change had happened in Kalpana. She attended Sampurna Mahila twice, the programme Harika madam conducted. Within a few months of meditation her arthritis reduced. Complaints about her mother-in-law, and about the other women of the house, loosened, and she came out of them. Only with her husband do quarrels remain. Small things trigger her. With everyone else she can understand and accept. Near him she feels her emotion is not understood, and shouting and crying follow. Later she goes into the room and meditates, and tells herself that this is his stage, that perhaps he is a man of knowledge who came for her sake. She sees it that way, and still cannot come out of the reaction. The burning stays: nirvana in the midst of samsara, Brahma-jnana, atmananda and Brahmananda, to teach and to share the self-knowledge she has, to balance household life and grow. That aspiration remains.","You have already overcome many things, Kalpana. The effort was made, the sadhana was done, and experiential knowledge came, which is why those earlier knots opened. The triggering around the husband will open too. If one sankalpa has been accomplished, the second is easy, and even a thousand can be. That confidence comes. One thing: regard the husband as a guru. The people who trigger us most are our gurus. There is a lesson of the soul in learning what has to be learned from them. The reaction is our experience, not theirs. It arose inside the ‘I’, and that has to be caught — why the trigger, why the loss of peace. Recognise what pain arises, and freedom from it is that awareness.","Those who praise us are never the gurus. Praise sticks us in one place. We swell, we go to cloud nine, and we fall under again. Those who trigger us are the real gurus, and with that feeling we can remain humble. Sadhana stays on. You are attending Jnanodayam even while doing pranayama, even from the car. Prasanna asked to share an experience, and was welcomed to do so when the time was there.","Kavita offered namaskarams to Sir, to Lakshmi madam, to the Quantum Life University sangha, and to everyone. Her son’s birthday had fallen the day before, which is why she had raised her hand. He was born on Mahanavami, and this year the 14th of October also came, so both would be kept. Someone had asked her whether the tithi or the calendar date was the one. The answer already given was that twice is even better, because that is what is done here.","Either way is ordinarily fine. Our roots are in India, not in a Western numerology that says the number of the birthday is the whole of it. That is very superficial. Dr. Newton was born on Kartika Purnima and celebrates that day with joy. It is the day he loves. For the world, the birth is the 24th of November — for Western countries, for the English reckoning. Here, the best is the tithi: the nakshatra, the lagna, the weekday, the day of birth. People born this way have a bonus of two birthdays. If enlightenment is attained, that day is a third birthday. We have been born anew. Good wishes to her son — a belated happy birthday. The time had reached 7:36. Tomorrow the others can share. We are in these Navaratri days in order to practise, and to learn the awakenings of sadhana. Thank you, friends. We meet again tomorrow morning at five."]$d5ens12json$::jsonb,
