insert into public.sections (id, day_id, section_order, title, content, minutes)
select
  'f95255fc-89d7-4e39-a165-1aead898e477'::uuid,
  d.id,
  1,
  $d6ens1title$Opening Meditation · The Empty Vessel$d6ens1title$,
  $d6ens1json$["Welcome to the 566th day of the Jnanodayam programme from Quantum Life University. For 566 days — almost more than a year and a half — we have been learning, through these Devi Navaratri days, the knowledge of the Devi and of that divine power. Brahmarshi Chakravarti Dr. Newton, founder and chairman, is himself conducting the classes, closing each day with a practice, and showing how the knowledge is to be lived.","Before the knowledge can be received, we have to become an empty vessel. So today, as on every other day, we sit for forty to forty-five minutes of meditation, and only then do we receive. Sit comfortably in sukhasana. Cross the legs, bring the fingers together, close the eyes, and with a small smile let the music play. Turn inward. Make the journey into yourself, and watch the breath — inhalation and exhalation, just as they are happening. When a thought comes, smile, and bring the attention back to the breath.","If the mind slides toward yoga nidra, return, and remain aware. For these forty minutes there is no other work. Watching the breath is the work.","In the final ten minutes this meditation and this knowledge are offered for the welfare of the world. Very soon a pyramid is to appear upon this earth. Let the light of knowledge at the Sahasrara, the crown, shine through the world and bring a feeling of unity in every person. Let this earth become a divine mandala. Let every living being live in oneness, joined to Prakriti, Nature, and moving in knowledge of the Self. We release that resolve into the universe with complete trust that it will take form.","On the 24th of November, 2027, we will gather and inaugurate this Sahasrara together. In a collective meditation, the true aim of the resolve — the play itself — begins. With this energy and this joy, bring the attention back to the breath, and stay joined to it.","For the last minute, remain with the breath. Five, four, three, two, one, zero. Slowly rest both hands over the eyes for a few moments. With a smile, open the eyes. Welcome again.","Today is the sixth day of Devi Navaratri. For five days an extraordinary knowledge has been coming. Whatever insights and realisations are shared across the whole of Jnanodayam were learned from Dr. Newton and from Lakshmi. To hear him directly, all the way through to Dashami, the tenth day, is the good fortune of everyone here. He is welcomed with a smile.","Dr. Newton thanks Harika, and wishes the friends of Jnanodayam a good morning. This is the sixth day. Holding these classes, staying inside the sadhana that belongs to them, and remaining in that state of energy: this is what matters. We return to it every day."]$d6ens1json$::jsonb,
  4
