insert into public.sections (id, day_id, section_order, title, content, minutes)
select
  '76a6bb6b-06ad-4156-a479-eb346ea3779e'::uuid,
  d.id,
  4,
  $d6ens4title$The Boon · Death Only Through the Mother$d6ens4title$,
  $d6ens4json$["When sadhana begins and the attention rests on the breath, on inhalation and exhalation, the sushumna, the central channel, becomes active, and the chakras open one by one. Sometimes a person has no experience at all of a chakra opening. At some moment the experiences of the third eye simply start. How can that be known? If the other chakras have not opened, the third eye does not open. For some people the energy arrives directly at the crown. Just as Mahishasura sat at the summit of Meru and meditated, many meditators feel the crown and enter the state of the Sahasrara.","At each centre, as each state is crossed, she herself is present — as Parashakti, the supreme power, and as Aparashakti, the power that works in the manifest world. As the energy rises into the higher centres, she herself becomes Parashakti. When the Sahasrara is reached, she is a power that gives birth to worlds, a power present everywhere. And yet each chakra has its own power. She herself is every one of those powers. She herself is the support of them all.","Mahishasura, out of his meditation, asks Brahma for a boon. He asks that he should die only through a woman. What he means is: I do not want death. I want to remain immortal. That cannot be given. Anyone who has put on this body — anyone who has put on this garment — must at some time vacate it. It is against the rule. A person may live twenty thousand years in a body, or thirty thousand, and still, at some time, the body has to be vacated and left.","Mahavatar Babaji is living now, embodied. Many live embodied. Many are chiranjivis, and many yogis of the Himalaya are among them. Even if one of them lived for a hundred thousand years, a day would come when the body had to be laid down. So Mahishasura is told to ask for a different boon. This one cannot stand. In the state of the Atman, deathlessness can be gained. A person can come to know: I am deathless; the Atman does not die. What cannot be had is the demand to remain in this body forever. This body will be left. It will certainly be left.","Then he says: I choose death through a woman. By the outer meaning, he is looking at woman as the lesser. By the inner meaning, only this Mother — Tripurasundari, Tribhuvaneshwari — can bring us to the Sahasrara at the crown. Without this Shakti we cannot move even an inch. We cannot meditate. We cannot do anything."]$d6ens4json$::jsonb,
