insert into public.sections (id, day_id, section_order, title, content, minutes)
select
  '3be0603a-ae95-45ac-a2e9-1d1a7aefe333'::uuid,
  d.id,
  5,
  $d6ens5title$Eighteen Arms · Weapons Against the Inner Enemy$d6ens5title$,
  $d6ens5json$["When she slays Mahishasura she is said to bear many weapons. In ancient India, people went to the ashrams and to the gurus in order to learn what these weapons are. Say Rama, and the arrow comes to mind. Say Krishna, and his discus comes to mind, the Sudarshana chakra, and with it the conch, the Panchajanya. Each divine power has a weapon — one, or two, or three, or four. There are many. Vishnu has his. Subrahmanya is called the lord of the spear, and the one who holds the staff. Hanuman too has weapons. He holds a mace, and it is said that a single stroke of that mace breaks even mountains into pieces and grinds them to powder.","Why should they need weapons? All of these are symbols. Outwardly, in a battle, there is a sword and a shield, and stranger instruments as well — something like a ball covered with thorns. They are the weapons that finish the inner enemies. Those enemies are in us, and Kundalini Mother is in us. Bearing the weapons, she brings that end about.","The Sudarshana chakra means seeing clearly. Through the chakra of the third eye, ignorance is cut away. What removes ignorance is the Sudarshana. Of Vishnu's two weapons, one is the conch and the other is the discus. The discus is the opened third eye, seeing well. The conch is sound, the nada of sound, and sound too is a weapon.","During the First World War, in Russia, many psychic experiments were made, and many experiments in parapsychology, among them experiments with sound. Without anyone knowing, ultrasonic waves were created — sounds that cannot even be heard — and sent upon the enemy camps, so that the soldiers would fall into depression, be seized by fear, and be unable to sleep. The experiment succeeded. It was used in a negative way, to stop an enemy: upon bases of war, upon an enemy kingdom, waves of sound were turned as a weapon. The same waves that can lift us can also drag us down.","She carries many weapons because Mahishasura will not keep one form. Once he is the buffalo. Before the trishula can pierce him, he has taken another form inside. He comes as a man, with a sword. He takes many forms after that. He becomes a lion. He becomes an elephant. It is said that he came in four forms, and so she begins to use the weapons, one after another.","The principal weapon is the trishula, and it came to her from Shiva, who bears it. The Sudarshana chakra came from Vishnu. The vajra, the thunderbolt that Indra holds, was given by Indra. The bow and the inexhaustible arrows came from Vayu, lord of the wind. The sword came from Yama. The mace was taken from Kubera. The shakti, a weapon like a spear, came from Agni. The noose and the conch were given by Varuna. The axe was given by Vishwakarma, the craftsman of the gods. With her eighteen arms she bears them all.","A change of form is the six inner enemies changing form. This is what the mind does. Its movements can look wholesome, and it changes shape so that we fail to recognise it. We think: all the anger in me left today. It has only changed face. It is still inside. The Mahishasura in us does the same, and we cannot even detect him. There is a stranger within, arriving in disguise. He is in everyone, including those who meditate.","Mahishasura also climbed Meru and sat in tapas at the summit. He too is a meditator, and the six are complete in him. Tamas is full, and rajas is there. Until those depart, and the defect of sattva with them, he cannot cross the three gunas or receive from the Mother what he is meant to receive. Kundalini awakening is not mere alertness. The whole process has to happen inside. In every meditator an inner war goes on. This Shakti takes the leading role, and in each chakra one inner enemy comes forward."]$d6ens5json$::jsonb,
