insert into public.sections (id, day_id, section_order, title, content, minutes)
select
  'faee95e1-97c5-41eb-acfd-2cfc7cbfbc2e'::uuid,
  d.id,
  6,
  $d6ens6title$Three Defects · The Trishula and the Fourth$d6ens6title$,
  $d6ens6json$["While we are at the Muladhara, the struggle is physical. It is survival. Enemies of that kind can be conquered when this Shakti is being known, when she is moving, when the awakening is happening at the level of the body.","Then comes the Swadhisthana, called the chakra of maya. Everything there is emotion, the surge of feeling. Dramas arrive — emotional dramas — and we are caught in them, badly caught. They do not end.","Crossing that centre, we come to the Manipura. Here we are meant to shine like a jewel. The Manipura has to blossom. What lives in it has to go: the trait of being the victim, the traits of the one who harms, the quality of injuring everyone, the principle of violence.","In each centre the Mother herself, as Shakti, fights. It is spoken of as a fierce battle. After the Anahata, the heart centre, is crossed, the movement enters the Vishuddha, the centre of the throat. Up to the Vishuddha she is Aparashakti. That Aparashakti then becomes Parashakti. Once the Ajna is crossed, she is Parashakti in a great measure. The Mother joins the Father. It is consciousness — pure consciousness.","Mahishasura, and the Mother who overcomes him, also mean mastery over animal nature. There is a great deal of it in us. Animals are not being slighted: they live by survival and carry many fears, and so do we. For the sake of survival there is room to slip into violence. When an animal is afraid, it attacks, and out of that fear it does harm.","We walk toward a snake and assume the fear is ours. In fact the snake is afraid of the human being: do not come near. If someone approaches without knowing, it bites. The violence is born from the fear, and fear is a form of ignorance. Those who are in knowledge cross fear first. As our own nature is known, fear is the first thing to leave.","Human beings carry the same animal nature. Tamas, rajas, and sattva, three defects, have hold of the jiva, the living being. Even a person strong in sattva comes to a defect: no one is as good as I am; I alone am good; everyone else is wicked; this whole world is wicked. He declares it to himself. This too has to be crossed. Mahishasura Mardini means the Shakti that removes all three.","Tamas comes first. Whatever is tied to bare survival, she breaks apart. Through tamas comes sleep, unconsciousness, a complete laziness, postponement, procrastination: I will do it tomorrow, tomorrow, tomorrow. We keep postponing ourselves. Rajas seizes us as well. Only the person who has crossed these understands. The body is needed, and while it is here the three are here and the experiences keep coming. Living beyond the three gunas means staying in the play, in contact, and yet not clinging.","As Kundalini Mother she abides in the Muladhara, and there she is first present as retas, the vital essence. The eight bodily constituents are spoken of alongside her. Eight arms name the Divine Mother who bears eight. Eighteen arms mean the five organs of knowledge, the five organs of action, and the eight constituents: the Mother present through all of them, the divine power that rules them. We have long heard of the seven dhatus. Speaking of them in the body, he names rasa, the plasma; rakta, the blood; mamsa, the muscle; medas, the fat; asthi, the bone; majja, the marrow; and shukra, the reproductive essence. When these are present, and rightly present, they become retas. Retas becomes ojas, the vital splendour. Ojas becomes tejas, radiance. Kundalini Shakti is first retas, then a great power as ojas, then light as tejas.","At the end she slays him with the trishula, and this too is a symbol. The trident speaks of the fourth state, the state that has crossed the three gunas. That is the inner meaning of the weapon. With it she destroys the three defects in Mahishasura, and the Kundalini Mother does the same in us. So we turn toward the state beyond the three gunas.","If the Shakti that supports this entire creation is not known, there is no spiritual progress. She has to be known. She is everywhere, and she is in us as Kundalini Shakti. Knowing her is not difficult. Whoever meditates comes to the experience of this Devi Shakti."]$d6ens6json$::jsonb,
  7
