insert into public.sections (id, day_id, section_order, title, content, minutes)
select
  '8ee28ad7-5848-4336-a1b3-4e53847ec2ea'::uuid,
  d.id,
  9,
  $d6ens9title$Four Stages · Salokya to Sayujya$d6ens9title$,
  $d6ens9json$["The Upanishads give a map. First, salokya: being in the same world. To know this Mother we must live in the loka where she is, and for that the fitness has to be earned. Meditation itself is the fitness. That is salokya. Then samipya, nearness: we draw closer to that Shakti.","Think of a Guru. First we hear of him, and the wish arises: I must meet him. Meeting him requires a fitness. The moment we arrive, he asks one thing: what is your question? We freeze. A thousand questions are waiting, and there is no time for them. He allows one question. A filter has to be passed. Fumble there, and he turns us away. Salokya is the earning of that fitness. To sit near him and learn, we have to be ready. It is like school. The earlier classes have to be completed before the tenth can be entered. In the same way, once a meditative state has come, salokya deepens into samipya and we move closer. Practice brings us closer still. We serve the Guru. Or we serve in the ashram, given over to seva.","Then sarupya, likeness of form. The manifestations of the Mother, her form, her qualities, are inculcated in us. We fill ourselves with them. The same happens with a Guru, and with Sri Krishna. His qualities enter us. Love toward everyone, a love without limit. When the cows appear he plays the flute. So much love in him toward Gomata, the mother cow: love, and love without end. Taking those qualities into ourselves is sarupya. In the language of our time it is role-modelling. What the Guru did, we also do. He practised meditation. If he sits for three hours, we sit for four.","Every disciple is to become a Guru on some day. In this world there are only two kinds of people: those who know, and those who do not. The ones who do not know must go and learn from the ones who know. Sayujya means you yourself become that. You become the Guru, and the sadhana continues.","The same four belong to Kundalini Mother. In salokya some fitness has been met and the practice is going on, but without devotion and attention — without vinaya, humility — it does not hold. Then samipya, then sarupya, then sayujya: we become as she is. At first what we see feels other than ourselves. Sayujya is oneness. She herself is you. You have become the Mother. Every meditator comes to this.","Today the four are practised, not only explained. Everyone wants a vision of the Mother, and it is said that she has no form and no name. We gave the names. If they are not known, Amma is enough. However she is called from the heart, she answers. She is Mother to everyone, Mother even of mothers, because she is the Mother of this creation. The process is simple. We try it now."]$d6ens9json$::jsonb,
