insert into public.sections (id, day_id, section_order, title, content, minutes)
select
  '322bb0ef-45e2-4e89-a0d3-7475d232175a'::uuid,
  d.id,
  10,
  $d6ens10title$Devi Samarpan · The Four Gears$d6ens10title$,
  $d6ens10json$["We begin with Devi Samarpan, the offering of oneself to the Mother. It is sharanagati. New friends are joining each day, so the practice is repeated for them. Someone may have come today for the first time. Toward that Shakti we are to be entirely in the feeling of offering, entirely in refuge. Kundalini Mother is already in us.","Even the way of sitting gives her importance. This is called Lakshmi mudra. Seated cross-legged, place the left leg on the right — outside, or above. The left leg rests upon the right. Then the breath: the left nostril, Chandra nadi, the lunar channel, and Chandra svara, the lunar current of the breath. That current is what leads us. Through it, draw the air in nine times, one inhalation after another, with no exhalation between them. Do not draw too deeply. Slowly: one, two, slowly. If the breath is quiet, all nine can be taken. Then hold gently.","Now join the hands in namaskara. In this land, namaskara is the culture itself. The two palms meet. What is held in that gesture is the feeling that I and you are one. Namaskara means Advaita. I, and the one before me, are not two. I bow to you. I bow to the Atman in you. To this Mother we say: I take refuge.","Slowly lower the head. Bend. The I-sense is surrendered completely. Everything is placed at her feet. This is samarpana. With the exhalation, releasing the air slowly, the floor may be touched. If it cannot, touch the ground with the hands. Stay there. Hold the breath out. Do not breathe in. Inwardly, in the mind alone, repeat Shrim nine times. Then slowly raise the head, bring the spine straight, and return to the first position. This is done nine times. That is Devi Samarpan. Those who finish — having offered pride, the sense of mine, and the blocks at her feet — sit in silence. The others complete their nine.","Then the four states are entered in the body, not only in explanation. Salokya, samipya, sarupya, sayujya. You are seated. You will sit in four directions, in four ways, like the four gears of a car.","For salokya, change posture and direction. Shift a little, and sit facing one way. This is the first gear, the gear of eligibility. To be fit for Lalita, for Tribhuvaneshwari, for the Mother of many names, what is required is devotion, attention, humility, and obedience. For one minute, eyes closed, feel the Kundalini Mother in you. Salokya here means a complete focus on the Shakti that drives us, drives the breath, and drives the whole creation. If attention, on a scale from one to ten, is sitting at five, move it to six, to seven, then eight, nine, ten. The offering has just been made. Now be joined to her.","Shift into the second gear. Change the direction, and sit another way. This is samipya. We are drawing near. The vibrations increase. If the Mother is close, how does that feel? She has no form. When that nirguna Shakti, the power without attributes, appears as saguna — with a name, with a form — and we are near, what is the feeling? Feel it completely, and remain in samipya for one minute. Going to the Himalaya, we meet the cool winds and drink them in. The coolness touches the skin. The vibration touches us. Nearness to this Adishakti, this Parashakti, is like that. The vibrations become known because we are close. She is not elsewhere. She is in us, and until now she was unrecognised. Recognise her. Come a little closer. The step is ours. We keep waiting for her to come to us. Let us go to her, as a child runs to the mother — Amma, Amma, Amma. We have to run.","The third direction is sarupya, the third gear. Change the posture again. Whatever qualities are hers, whatever vibration, whatever form of Shakti, integrate them within. The feeling of this third state is that she and we are not other. Her qualities are filling us. As Aparashakti, this same power is of use in ordinary life. Many things can be brought into being through her. Many obstacles can be removed. Victories come through this Shakti alone. Tune to her completely, and then more completely.","The fourth direction is sayujya. Change once more. Sayujya means that you become the Mother herself. Put on the form of the power on whom this creation runs: Mahishasura Mardini, the trishula in her hand, many weapons, eighteen arms. We too hold the trishula. The trishula is tamas, rajas, and sattva crossed — the state beyond the three gunas, and the state beyond waking, dream, and deep sleep, which is Turiya. Become the Mother who bears it.","Tune completely. Until now the Mother was seen from outside. Now let Mother and ourselves be one. Once, we were one. As an infant in the womb, as an embryo, we were not other than our mother. We are in that same state of ekatva, oneness. Become that Mother. Observe the energy. In the hand, symbolically, imagine a trishula, and feel what it is to hold it. Remain in this feeling: I am the Shakti who has crossed the defects of tamas, rajas, and sattva, and who stands beyond the three gunas. I am the Shakti who has crossed waking, dream, and sleep, and who stands in Turiya. The Mother and I are one. Stay in that energy, in that posture, for one minute. Then, slowly, return to the waking state."]$d6ens10json$::jsonb,
