insert into public.sections (id, day_id, section_order, title, content, minutes)
select
  '95a99f44-a3db-409a-a300-86a454358209'::uuid,
  d.id,
  11,
  $d6ens11title$The Hymn · The Surge Is Not Danger$d6ens11title$,
  $d6ens11json$["Harika then offers a hymn to Sri Rajarajeshwari. The line that returns asks the compassionate Mother, she whose nature is pure consciousness, for protection: Sri Rajarajeshwari sadaye chinmatrike pahi mam. She is addressed as Tripurasundari in the chakra that is all bliss, as Shiva-Shankari of peaceful essence, as the one formed of the five Brahmas, and as Satchidananda. He receives the hymn and turns to those who wish to speak.","One friend says that speaking with him feels like good fortune. For a long time he has been singing a song whose words are salokya and samipya — are these not of this very world? — and no one had ever told him what the words mean. Today the meaning arrived, and the joy with it. He speaks also of Durga. He had watched cocks, and other animals, being sacrificed before her, and had lived with the feeling: why should she be worshipped at all? Across these nine days, and in the detail of this class, he has been learning who she is. Every day he is practising with the feeling of samarpana. He says he will come of his own accord on the 24th of November, to serve. He is welcomed. Come. Seva is the way.","Dhana speaks next. He met Dr. Newton in person for the first time in Hyderabad, at the national gathering for ahimsa, non-violence, and the meeting itself made him happy. These six days of class he is able to feel, and he is taking up what has been said. There is ego even at the subtle level, and in the sadhana of offering, a great part of it leaves. With his mother he is now able to speak without violence. A real connection is forming. Even when she scolds, somewhere in it there is love, and if that love is held, the connection becomes easy.","His question is about the beginning of meditation, and about the udvrtti, the upsurge. He used to be afraid when it came. What is this? At that time the knowledge was not yet in place. He would be frightened, and he would scold himself: why is this Shakti giving so much trouble? Now, however strong the upsurge, he is happy. However much force arrives, it feels as though something is being repaired, and he is at ease. The Mother who slew Mahishasura — are these inner blocks even worth counting? They will go. To that extent he has surrendered, and the fear is no longer there. Even in sleep, dreams are coming, and he is watching them clearly. The practice of the gears, from the first through to the last, went completely in. It amazes him.","Dr. Newton answers that the knowledge being learned is being integrated. First there is shravana, hearing. Then manana, reflection. Then nididhyasana, deep contemplation. What is learned has to become anubhava, a lived experience, an inner feeling. Only when it arises inside is it truly gained, and that is why these states are being reached. However intense the upsurge, a great understanding has come with it: this is not danger. It is a safe feeling — the safest feeling of all. Many people are badly afraid of the surging of Parashakti, badly afraid of the rising of Kundalini. She is the kindest master. She is a master with the quality of a mother. The integration is wonderful.","A smaller doubt follows. While the process is happening, the body grows tired. He tells himself he will get up and sit again, and the moment he thinks it, relaxation comes. It feels as though he is being told: all right, come back; we will see each other again. Is this all right? It is all right. After a deep state, the pull to return to the outside is natural. What is asked is that the moment be prolonged — one minute, two minutes. Do not come out at once. Remain a little, and return gradually. Never snap back into fear, and never come back in a hurry. It is a brink. The moment is very precious. Sometimes it has to be held. We speak of walking one extra mile. In sadhana, one extra minute. The level of tolerance has to rise. It will feel like time to come back. Wait one minute more. In that single minute, a great deal happens."]$d6ens11json$::jsonb,
