insert into public.sections (id, day_id, section_order, title, content, minutes)
select
  '936a60f1-8624-4147-aab8-c9f6b168a8f9'::uuid,
  d.id,
  2,
  $d7ens2title$Saptami · The Sword of Knowledge$d7ens2title$,
  $d7ens2json$["Jnanodayam. Good morning. Wonderful, my dear friends. Today is Saptami, the seventh day. Saptami, Ashtami, and Navami, the last three days of Navaratri, are felt and celebrated as very great, and there is a reason. The fruits of the sadhana we have been doing come into experience in these three days. In the first six days we have already spoken of what that sadhana is.","We spoke of iccha shakti, kriya shakti, and jnana shakti — the powers of will, of action, and of knowledge — and of Mahadurga, Mahalakshmi, and Mahasaraswati. These last three days belong to Mahasaraswati, the form of knowledge. An inner purification has been going on, and this too is purification. It happens now through the sword called knowledge.","The stories we have been using are those of the Devi Bhagavatam, written by Maharshi Markandeya in the Markandeya Purana, and the narratives of the Devi Mahatmyam. We have been learning them with their inner meaning. How Mahishasura was slain became a way of speaking about the enemies inside us. Every one of these stories is telling us a single thing.","Taken only on the outside, a story gives a little entertainment and a little joy, because a story is being heard, and nothing more. The benefit is in the inner meaning. These tales were written full of it. Today we take up the stories that carry the same teaching further. Many asuras were destroyed by the divine power, by Kalika, by Chandi, under many names. Read as symbols, they are the inner enemies. With the power in us that has been awakened, we destroy them first in ourselves."]$d7ens2json$::jsonb,
  2
