insert into public.sections (id, day_id, section_order, title, content, minutes)
select
  '35be7785-b690-448e-a6b4-bc8627e74a7e'::uuid,
  d.id,
  3,
  $d7ens3title$Sumbha and Nisumbha · Pleasure, Pain, and the Four$d7ens3title$,
  $d7ens3json$["Sumbha and Nisumbha are called brothers, and they stand as a pair. In the sadhaka, Sumbha is the circling tendency of the pleasure-impression, and Nisumbha the tendency of sorrow. They are vrittis. The word has to be heard carefully: vritta means a circle. Pleasure and pain spin us and do not leave one another. In pain we resolve upon pleasure; when pleasure comes, pain comes back. We ask why the pain comes if the pleasure was what we wanted. The root is ahankara and mamakara, the sense of I and the sense of mine.","These are mental tendencies seated in the subconscious, always turning: I want this, I want that, and the mind leans toward pleasure, and pain arrives with it. In the story Sumbha is a king and Nisumbha his brother, and it is said that Nisumbha was destroyed fighting Indra. Others then entered Sumbha's court: Chanda, Munda, Dhumralochana, and Raktabija. We have heard of Raktabija before. When Karambha was seized upon his own funeral pyre, he came out again as Raktabija. All of this is symbol.","If the circles of pleasure and pain are in us, and if I and mine are there, the others come and join them. The bad qualities arrive in a crowd. Chanda is deceit, a frightening crookedness of mind. We cheat ourselves; that is self-deception. Munda is the tendency that wrecks everything. Mundana is the clean shaving of the head, and in the inner sense it is destruction: self-sabotage. We do all that success requires, and then we destroy ourselves. We climb ninety-nine steps and fall at the ninety-ninth.","Dhumralochana: dhumra is smoke. In smoke nothing ahead can be seen. This is the tendency of maya, which makes what exists seem absent and what is absent seem to exist. Raktabija is the subtle ego. One drop of his blood on the ground becomes a thousand of him. Even a fine ahankara breeds Raktabijas without end. They all joined Sumbha's court. Where pleasure and pain, I and mine, are kept, these others arrive without a limit.","We meditate every day, with the help of this Shakti, in order to win over those inner enemies. Meditation is how the power is gathered. We do not misuse what is in us. We connect with it, and we trust the Mother completely."]$d7ens3json$::jsonb,
