insert into public.sections (id, day_id, section_order, title, content, minutes)
select
  'e954db6e-3809-4f67-a60f-fbdebd33538e'::uuid,
  d.id,
  4,
  $d7ens4title$The Golden Image · Ego and the Spiritual Mask$d7ens4title$,
  $d7ens4json$["Trust and surrender go together. Without trust there is no surrender, and no sharanagati, no taking of refuge. We do not trust the power that is already in us, yet that power does what we cannot do by ourselves. This is why meditation is spoken of. Through it the power is awakened, and the power does the work. Its first work is to finish the inner enemies. Sumbha and Nisumbha, Chanda and Munda, Raktabija and Dhumralochana are in this life. Only the inner meaning gives the clarity, and the sword of knowledge, by which they are conquered.","Begin with the ahankara and mamakara that manufacture our pleasure and our pain. There is gross ego, and there is subtle ego, and both have to be recognised. A story. In a village a great sculptor carved a golden image so well that he thought: there is no sculptor like me in the world. Excellence in a profession brings this. It comes without our noticing. It comes among meditators. Sumbha and Nisumbha were practisers. Mahishasura, whom we have already studied, did tapas. Seekers of knowledge are not exempt.","The danger is the spiritual mask. I meditate, I meditate — and the ego is large, and nothing has changed. The same anger, the same tendencies, the same self-destruction. Families see it. The more meditation is talked about, the further they step back. First change yourself, they say, and then I will believe you. The mask is worn without our knowing. Ego and mamakara sit in us, subtle and subtler.","After the golden image, a sadhu came to the sculptor's house. Proudly the images were shown. See how finely I have made them, Swami; see my skill. The sadhu laughed, and pointed to a small clay lamp in a corner. My son, these golden figures are beautiful, but drop them and they break, and thieves may carry them off at any time. This clay lamp takes the darkness away and bears the light. It has no pride, no fear, no ego. Your ego is like the golden image. It can shatter at any moment. Light the clay lamp of Self-knowledge.","Pride of that kind says there is no hero like me, and no sun. The shapes of it are many."]$d7ens4json$::jsonb,
