insert into public.sections (id, day_id, section_order, title, content, minutes)
select
  'e00ef6e8-cbce-445b-aca0-814f36c48fa1'::uuid,
  d.id,
  5,
  $d7ens5title$Ahankara · Doership and the Throat$d7ens5title$,
  $d7ens5json$["There is the ego of money. Without money we are one person; after it arrives we are another. A post arrives, a status, and ego comes with it. There is ego about beauty, and intellectual arrogance: the PhD, the gold medal, the feeling of knowing more than everyone, the degrees, the English well spoken. Education can be an ego, and so can wealth. Birth in a caste or a lineage is an ego too, once we identify with it and look down. So is the claim that no one is stronger, or more in the flush of youth.","Sadhana itself grows an ego. I have meditated for thirty years, and that person for ten; I have done this for thirty-five years; I am the senior. A subtle ego. The count is not the years. It is the quality of the sitting. Many have practised a long time, in a general way, and have not moved, because the knowledge was not what they grasped. Grasp the ego, and it spins you. A vritti is a circle. It repeats, and we fall back into it.","When we are in the higher worlds we think: these tendencies are mine; this time I will break the pattern. We choose a design for the life. We are born, and we fall into the same pit. It is like the pit on the path away from the house. We fell once. We say, this time I will not, and we walk carefully, and we fall into it again. Birth after birth. Chiefly it is ahankara: I did all of this. That is the ego of doership. No one, we feel, could have done it better.","True service is done with no sense of being the doer. Some people do not know that dimension. They want to be praised, to have it recognised that they served, to be known for it in society. That too is ego. Spirituality means becoming zero, shunya, because these are what stop us. Otherwise we rise as far as the vishuddha, the centre at the throat, and fall back beneath it. To go above, I and mine have to be released. If they are not, the energy stays below the throat. The whole of life is lived there. We do not reach ajna, the centre above, and the energy is lost where we are."]$d7ens5json$::jsonb,
