insert into public.sections (id, day_id, section_order, title, content, minutes)
select
  '3dacfd43-9a04-459b-af19-842c8e09259a'::uuid,
  d.id,
  10,
  $d7ens10title$Devi Samarpan · Nine Breaths and the Hymn$d7ens10title$,
  $d7ens10json$["Let us do the Devi Samarpan we practise each day. Place the left foot on the right. The alignment is with the energy; through these nine days we stay aligned with that dimension. Through the chandra nadi, the lunar channel, take nine breaths in. Close the right nostril and inhale nine times, slowly. Do not breathe out between them, and do not pull hard. After the ninth, pause, and gather the breath a little. Then join the palms in namaskara.","Do the rest with the feeling of offering. We are surrendering to Jagadamba, the Mother of the world, and to the dimension of energy, with sharanagati, the feeling of refuge, and with complete trust. Bow the head. Let the air out slowly, and touch the ground if you can. If you cannot, that is enough. In that gap, as in kumbhaka, the pause where the breath is held, do not take a breath. Inwardly, nine times, say the bija Shrim — the seed-sound of the Mother. Then bring the head back up, and while rising fill the breath in. Nine rounds, for the nine nights. Those who have finished, remain in silence. Those who have not, continue.","While that goes on, Harika madam sang a hymn of the Mother — of Ambika, Mahasaraswati, Mahagauri, and Mahalakshmi. It opens: Varavīṇā mṛdupāṇi vanaruhalochanā rāṇi — the queen of the excellent veena, the soft hand, the lotus eyes. Every day her music fills that energy in all of us. And then a few people shared."]$d7ens10json$::jsonb,
  2
