insert into public.sections (id, day_id, section_order, title, content, minutes)
select
  'a529c19d-835f-466e-a40b-87106d866d4e'::uuid,
  d.id,
  12,
  $d7ens12title$The Inner Master · An Extra Hour on Saptami$d7ens12title$,
  $d7ens12json$["Krishna Chaitanya was outside, and left the video off so that the question could be held in focus. What is the difference between coming to know the truth and being caught in over-analysis? From childhood, whenever the atma was spoken of, it could not be seen, and so it was skipped, and many things were skipped in the same way. A daughter of thirteen had recently said: you listen to so many classes and learn so much; if you cannot see it, that does not mean it is not there. It means you have not seen it yet. How to receive that was not clear.","The question went on. We keep saying that inner-child blocks must be removed, and wounds, and traumas. One apparent truth after another is uncovered, and none of them is the Truth. Then there is a life purpose. A process from the day before had been missed, and would be written down from the video and done. When Jamila was asked what brings contentment of the Self, a further doubt appeared: do we design the life purpose as we come here? If the block is a truth, and the trauma, and what was brought from the parents, and the family constellation, which of them is the truth? What is final? Where is the line between a life purpose and the search for truth?","The daughter is a wonderful master. Not seeing a thing does not mean it is absent. We are the ones who cannot see, and this is true of many things. It is also not true that everyone carries inner blocks. Some may. Some may not. What we can understand is our own life. Difficulties come. Emotions come. We react, we are triggered, and behind that are inner enemies, which we are calling blocks. They count as present because the world mirrors us, and we estimate ourselves from the reflection. In meditation we can see what has to be set right. A word comes out hollow. An emotion is expressed. We sink, we suffer, we take every remark personally. That personal taking is subtle ego. Someone spoke from their own emotional state; we heard it as ours, because the ego is still there. These are wounds. They are not a rule.","Hard circumstances do not write the same wound in everyone. Think of thirty children whose parents were not there, left with a grandmother while the parents went abroad to earn. Distance from the parents does not plant a block in all thirty. In five, or in ten, it may. It depends on how the thing is interpreted. On this path the requirement is to be open, and to watch. Self-observation shows what is still there: ego, mamakara, a place that hurts, a reaction, a void. Where did the void come from? From whatever was not received in childhood. We then search for it outside. Freedom was refused, and only restrictions were given, so now freedom is hunted in the world. Approval was not given, so now we wait to be approved and appreciated. Seeing this is part of the purification. Do not decide beforehand that the blocks are there. See the life. Feelings are indicators. With a little meditation, thoughts can be seen as well. They pass like waves. At first the feelings are what everyone can catch. Behind an emotion is a thought, behind the thought a belief, behind the belief a memory, a past that has to be understood and set right. From that, a sadhaka knows what change to bring. Do not generalise that blocks are universal.","Krishna was born in a prison. Did the blocks come to him? He was born a master, with knowledge, and there was no inner-child block in him. From childhood, rakshasas and dramas, and not one of them touched him. Through a hundred and twenty years, a hundred and thirty, people came to destroy him, and every day was a hell, and he was joyful. He had no blocks. Our own awareness is what tells us about ourselves. The spiritual mask is related. Many say that all is well, and live as escapists, running from problems into sannyasa: I will not carry these responsibilities; I will renounce and go. That is not the path. Meditation means facing, with this power, whatever problem or challenge has come, and resolving it. Knowledge gives the strength to do that. The mask that says everything is fine is a defence. Be open. Do not sit wondering how many unseen blocks you must be carrying. Simply be open.","Then the question was put plainly. Searching for a root cause is not over-analysis, is it? Only if there is a problem. If there is no problem, a root cause is not required. Where difficulty and sorrow are actually happening, look for the cause. Where they are not, there is nothing to dig up. Then go toward knowledge, and do the sadhana. Along the way, blocks do appear. Procrastination, laziness, a practice that will not stay steady: that is a block. So is the feeling of being less. Everyone else meditates well; I cannot; I am not good enough; I am inferior. That is an inner block, and it has to be overcome, because every person is a great master. Around the inner master, layer on layer has covered what is there. Recognise the layers.","The remaining questions, from Lakshmi Kalyan and from Swapnajyoti, can wait until tomorrow. Today is Durga Saptami, a sacred day. Add an hour to the meditation. Walk the extra mile. In sadhana, stay a step ahead. We have talked a great deal. Without experience the talk is nothing. Sit. Sit in silence. Sit still. We meet again tomorrow morning.","Whoever wishes to be on Zoom will see a QR code after this; the slide can be shared. Scan it and join the WhatsApp community, where a post goes up every day. Divya may share the slide. There are courses, and many activities at Quantum Life University. The One Maitriya programme is held every month; the details and the codes are on the website. If you are with us on YouTube, like the videos and share them with people you know. You may also contribute toward the courses. One Maitriya itself is on the 24th and 25th of October. Dr. Newton and Lakshmi will be there, and whenever he can, Sir takes a class himself. It is usually a Saturday, and it begins at five in the morning, so come on Friday evening. The dates of the later gatherings are on the slide. Plan from them. Thank you. Tomorrow morning at five. Om."]$d7ens12json$::jsonb,
