insert into public.sections (id, day_id, section_order, title, content, minutes)
select
  'f288a8d3-3428-4a16-a5b1-39938c7d4f6b'::uuid,
  d.id,
  1,
  $d8ens1title$Opening Meditation · Anapanasati$d8ens1title$,
  $d8ens1json$["Welcome to the 568th day of the Jnanodayam programme conducted by Quantum Life University. Today is also the eighth day of Devi Navaratri. Every day we are receiving this knowledge directly from our Guru, Dr. Newton. We are celebrating the Devi Navaratri days beautifully through sadhana.","While learning about sadhana, we are also understanding how much it is useful in life. Every day, under the direct guidance and supervision of the Guru, we are practising. Today also, before Dr. Newton arrives, let us begin with meditation practice. The meditation we do is Anapanasati meditation — a simple process. Sit comfortably in a stable posture.","You may sit on the floor or on a chair. Place the thumb and forefinger together, cross the legs if possible, remove glasses if you are wearing them, close the eyes, and simply observe the natural flow of the breath for the next 45 minutes. There is no need to engage with any thoughts, and no need to engage with the outer world. All our attention is only on the inner journey — on the breath.","We simply observe the breath as it is. Soft music is playing. Whenever a thought arises in between, with a gentle smile we bring the attention back to the breath. Om… Om… Om… In the final 10 minutes, let us use this meditative energy for the welfare of all.","Bring the attention to the top of the head — the Sahasrara region — and experience the light of knowledge there. This energy, this light of knowledge, slowly flows like a stream from the top of the head throughout the body. This same energy is present in all of us, in every living being, in every object, and all around us. It is nourishing all of us.","Feel this energy flowing from the crown of the head downward, purifying and illuminating every part. Let the awareness remain soft and steady. No effort is needed — only gentle observation and offering.","As the meditation deepens, the sense of a separate observer begins to soften. What remains is simply the flow of breath and the presence of awareness. This is the natural state we are returning to each day through practice.","In these final moments, offer the entire meditation — the stillness, the breath, and whatever has arisen — to the Mother. Let it benefit all beings.","Slowly bring the awareness back. When you are ready, gently open the eyes with a smile. Welcome once again."]$d8ens1json$::jsonb,
