insert into public.sections (id, day_id, section_order, title, content, minutes)
select
  'b2a4f64d-ba56-42ed-a83e-aa7d393414cf'::uuid,
  d.id,
  2,
  $d8ens2title$Devi Shakti · Respect for Nature$d8ens2title$,
  $d8ens2json$["Welcome back everyone. Today we have reached the eighth day. The outer Dussehra holidays may be over, but the inner celebration continues. If everyone is ready to receive the knowledge, please turn on your cameras and, with a smile, let us welcome our Guru — Brahmarshi Chakravarti Dr. Newton Kondaveti.","Thank you, Sir, for being here today. Over to you. Dear friends of Jnanodayam, today we have arrived at Ashtami — the eighth day of Navaratri sadhana. Devi Navaratri was instituted only for sadhana. Through this practice, and through the power of Devi Shakti, we are to bring about whatever changes are needed within ourselves.","Today’s focus is the reverence we must have toward Prakriti — Nature. Devi is Prakriti. When we respect Nature, we are respecting the Mother. Every element — earth, water, fire, air, and space — is Her form.","When we pollute or misuse the elements, we are disrespecting Her. The sadhana of this day is to consciously honour the five elements and the Mother who is present as them.","Every morning when we wake up, the first act can be a simple recognition: the air we breathe is Her, the water we drink is Her, the earth that supports us is Her. This recognition itself is worship.","In the outer world we see so much disregard for Nature. But the change begins within. When the sadhaka begins to see Devi in every form of Prakriti, his relationship with the world transforms.","The five elements are not outside us. They are the very substance of the body and mind. Honouring them is honouring the body-temple in which the Mother dwells.","Today, as part of the practice, let us consciously offer gratitude to the five elements. Even a few moments of sincere recognition changes the quality of the day.","Devi Shakti is not separate from the world. She is the power that moves everything. When we align with Her through respect and surrender, that same power begins to work for our inner transformation.","The eighth day reminds us that knowledge without reverence remains incomplete. Reverence toward Prakriti is the foundation on which true knowledge stands.","Whatever we do today — eating, walking, speaking — can be done with the awareness that it is happening within the Mother’s field. This is practical sadhana.","Many people wait for special occasions to remember the Divine. But the Mother is available in every breath and every element. The eighth day invites us to remember this continuously.","When the mind is restless, return to the elements. Feel the solidity of the earth, the coolness of water, the warmth of fire, the movement of air, the spaciousness of space. Each one can bring the mind back.","This is not philosophy. It is a living practice. The more we honour Prakriti, the more the inner Prakriti — the mind and emotions — begins to settle.","Dr. Newton often says that the outer world is a reflection of the inner state. When we begin to treat Nature with reverence, the inner nature also starts responding with greater clarity and peace.","Let this eighth day be a day of conscious reverence. Even small acts done with awareness become offerings.","Now, with this understanding, let us continue the sadhana of the day."]$d8ens2json$::jsonb,
