insert into public.sections (id, day_id, section_order, title, content, minutes)
select
  '953e8e5f-7469-4556-ab4e-7335b4107bed'::uuid,
  d.id,
  3,
  $d8ens3title$Anger · The Power of Words$d8ens3title$,
  $d8ens3json$["There was a small boy whose father noticed that he had a lot of anger. Whenever he became angry, he would shout and create a lot of noise. To help the boy develop awareness of his anger, the father said: ‘Whenever you get angry, there is an empty wall in our house. Drive a nail into that wall.’","So every time anger arose, the boy would immediately go and hammer a nail into the wall. On the first day alone he drove 36 nails — meaning he became angry 36 times. He continued this process for several days. Gradually, awareness of anger increased.","Later the father said: ‘Now, whenever you control your anger, pull one nail out.’ Over time the wall became full of holes. The father then showed him: ‘See, even after the nails are removed, the holes remain. In the same way, angry words leave scars even after the anger is gone.’","This is the teaching: words spoken in anger create lasting impressions. Awareness is the first step. Once awareness is there, the power to choose differently appears.","In sadhana, anger is not suppressed. It is seen. When it is seen clearly, its power to control us reduces. The nail story is a simple method to develop that seeing.","Today, whenever anger or irritation arises, instead of reacting immediately, pause and notice it. That pause itself is the beginning of freedom."]$d8ens3json$::jsonb,
