insert into public.sections (id, day_id, section_order, title, content, minutes)
select
  '526155bf-8e31-4ba4-ae0c-0b6713b5eca3'::uuid,
  d.id,
  5,
  $d8ens5title$Mahasaraswati · Self-Knowledge$d8ens5title$,
  $d8ens5json$["On this eighth day we also remember Mahasaraswati. She is the form of knowledge. True Self-knowledge is not information; it is the direct seeing of one’s own nature.","Saraswati’s veena represents the harmony that appears when the mind becomes still and the light of knowledge shines without obstruction.","Knowledge that remains only in the intellect does not transform. Knowledge that is lived becomes wisdom. Saraswati blesses both, but the second is the real fruit.","In the Navaratri sadhana, each day corresponds to a deepening. The eighth day invites us to let knowledge settle into being.","Many seekers collect teachings. Few allow the teachings to dissolve the collector. That dissolution is the work of Saraswati’s grace.","When the mind is full of concepts, even true concepts become obstacles. The practice is to use the concept and then release it.","Mahasaraswati is also the power of speech that is aligned with truth. When speech becomes truthful and non-harming, it becomes an instrument of knowledge.","Today, observe your speech. Is it creating clarity or confusion? Even this observation is part of the sadhana.","Offer the faculty of speech and the desire for knowledge to the Mother. Let them be purified."]$d8ens5json$::jsonb,
