insert into public.sections (id, day_id, section_order, title, content, minutes)
select
  'ce98de5d-5931-4dfe-a26d-085fdec7295b'::uuid,
  d.id,
  9,
  $d8ens9title$The Devi Chant · Shared Experiences$d8ens9title$,
  $d8ens9json$["Harika madam then led a beautiful chant: Yā Devī sarva-bhūteṣu Viṣṇumāyeti śabditā. Namastasyai namastasyai namastasyai namo namaḥ.","Every line of this chant carries deep meaning. It is not merely an external namaskara to the Mother. It is the recognition that all states of life — longing, energy, peace, anxiety, hope, indifference, light, wealth, memory, compassion, contentment, the form of the Mother, delusion, activity, Prakriti itself — are Her forms.","When we listen to or chant this, we are acknowledging that everything we experience is the Mother appearing in different ways.","After the chant, participants shared their experiences from the previous days of sadhana — the effect of the practices, the shifts in the mind, and the growing sense of surrender.","One participant spoke of how the daily Samarpan had reduced the intensity of old reactions. Another mentioned a greater sense of quiet even in the midst of work.","These sharings are not for comparison. They are reminders that the practices work in ordinary lives, not only in ideal conditions.","Each person’s experience is unique, yet the underlying movement is the same: a gradual loosening of identification and a growing trust in the Mother’s presence.","Dr. Newton listened and occasionally clarified points, emphasising that consistency matters more than dramatic experiences.","The chant and the sharings together create a field in which the individual practice is supported by the collective.","Even those who only listened reported feeling a quieting of the mind. This is the power of sincere collective sadhana.","The eighth day thus combined clear teaching, direct practice, and the living testimony of fellow sadhakas.","Such a combination is rare and precious. It is the hallmark of this Navaratri series.","As the session moved toward its close, the atmosphere remained one of quiet gratitude.","Many expressed the intention to continue the practices beyond the nine days.","This intention itself is Shubheccha — the first plane — renewing itself.","The chant continued to resonate in the background as people prepared to leave the session.","In the traditional understanding, the sound of the Devi’s names continues to work even after the audible chant has ended.","Participants were encouraged to carry one line of the chant into the day and repeat it softly whenever remembered.","This simple continuation links the formal session with ordinary life.","The sharings also revealed that many had begun to see daily difficulties as part of the sadhana rather than as obstacles to it.","This shift in perspective is one of the practical fruits of the teaching.","With these reflections, the main body of the session came to a close.","The final announcements followed."]$d8ens9json$::jsonb,
  7
