insert into public.sections (id, day_id, section_order, title, content, minutes)
select
  '48e18c00-ccfd-4106-a6e9-188d3e2f3dac'::uuid,
  d.id,
  1,
  $d9ens1title$Opening Meditation · Anapanasati$d9ens1title$,
  $d9ens1json$["Welcome to the 569th day of the Jnanodayam programme, and to the ninth day of Navaratri. We have almost come to the end. Tomorrow is the Dussehra celebration. How fortunate we all are. Each morning of these nine days we have been learning this Navaratri knowledge from Dr. Newton. Today too, let us become ready to receive it. Let us sit well in meditation for about forty-five minutes, and after that receive the knowledge.","The practice we all do is Anapanasati. It is a very simple method. Sit comfortably in a steady posture. You may sit on a chair and take the support of the back, or, if you wish, sit on the floor. Cross the feet. Those seated on a chair, rest the fingers on the knees. Close both eyes, and with a small smile watch the breath as it happens naturally.","Soft music will be playing. Whenever a thought comes, that music reminds us. It brings our attention back to the breath. We watch the breath exactly as it is. Without any other thought, we remain with this breath alone. Wherever the breath leads us, we go that way. This is an inner journey, a journey we make into ourselves.","Om. Om. Om.","Simply watching, we witness all of it. In this state of meditation, let us offer our power of knowledge and our sankalpa for a blessing. May this earth become a field of peace, of knowledge, and of power. Holding the Self that is in every person, let us invite the Sahasrara that is taking form at Quantum Life University, the Sahasrara of the lamp of knowledge.","May compassion and joy be tended with care. Let us take the sankalpa that what is natural in all of us may live in kinship with every living being on this earth. At the lotus of a thousand petals, and in its midst, together with the many secret geometric forms, we share all of this. Together we are meditating. Let us experience our true nature directly, and release this sankalpa to the universe. Seeing how wonderfully this has happened, bring the attention back, in every moment, to the breath.","One minute remains. Five, four, three, two, one, zero. Slowly rest both hands over the eyes for a few moments. With a small smile, let us open the eyes."]$d9ens1json$::jsonb,
  3
