insert into public.sections (id, day_id, section_order, title, content, minutes)
select
  'a607bcbc-6520-489c-afe0-c186079f22a2'::uuid,
  d.id,
  3,
  $d9ens3title$The First Principle · Shakti, Chaitanya, Knowledge$d9ens3title$,
  $d9ens3json$["Today let us learn seven principles about this Shakti. The Divine Mother, the Mother of the world, Adishakti, has made herself known in many forms. If we are to say it in scientific language, we call her Shakti. We see the Mother of the world as the form of energy.","Through meditation, Shakti. Through Shakti, Chaitanya. Through Shakti and Chaitanya, knowledge. This is the first principle. Whoever comes into meditation, this is the first thing we say. Meditate. You must fill yourself well with energy. First we invoke the cosmic energy. That cosmic energy flows in us. Once we are in a state free of thought, the Kundalini Shakti hidden within us also awakens. This Shakti comes to us through meditation. Principally, it comes through meditation.","Without this Shakti we cannot even understand Chaitanya. Of this whole creation we say that it arose from the union of Shakti and Chaitanya. We say that the whole creation is the union of Purusha and Prakriti. Prakriti itself is Shakti, that divine power. Chaitanya itself is Purusha. In this way our texts speak in symbols. When the union of Shakti and Chaitanya takes place, from the Ajna chakra, knowledge comes in us. The union of Shakti and Chaitanya is knowledge. This is the first principle. It is a principle everyone can understand.","After a person has come into meditation, this is the first point we give. This is the process that happens in every meditator. First Shakti. That Shakti itself leads toward Chaitanya. Chaitanya means remaining still, always in awareness. It is stillness, absolute stillness. If we look at Ishvara, we understand. Look at Parama Shiva. He is always seated in meditation, perfectly still.","Mother Parvati and Parama Shiva, and the sons of those two, Ganapati and Kumaraswami, are both forms of knowledge. The son of Shiva, born of Mother Parvati. We speak of the sons born to Shiva in this symbolic language, in a way everyone can understand. What we learn here in spiritual science, in the science of the Self, is this. Knowledge arises, knowledge is born, knowledge comes, from the union of Shakti and Chaitanya. Here it is not ordinary knowledge. It is not worldly knowledge. It is parajnana, knowledge belonging to the Self.","We contemplate that as Jnana Subrahmanya and as Jnana Vighneshwara. All of these are symbolic forms. This is the first principle, friends."]$d9ens3json$::jsonb,
  3
