insert into public.sections (id, day_id, section_order, title, content, minutes)
select
  '19b36cd3-8a2e-4c36-a256-440fe48c875f'::uuid,
  d.id,
  4,
  $d9ens4title$The Second Principle · Give the Shakti a Direction$d9ens4title$,
  $d9ens4json$["The second. We practise for nine days in these Navaratri days because the flow of that Shakti is very strong. Twice in the year this divine energy moves in this way. These nine days are the Sharad Navaratri, the Devi Navaratri that comes every year in September and October. Once more, in the month of April, with Sri Ramanavami, another Navaratri comes. At both of these times the availability of that Shakti is very great.","The Shakti we are receiving in this Navaratri practice, the Shakti that is being activated still more in us, must be given a direction. We must see in which direction that Shakti goes. Otherwise it is put to good use once, and misused another time. That is why these Navaratri days are here. The direction has to be set.","Let us speak of it as flowing in two directions. The second point is this. When we practise with great care, intensely, with some intensity, that Shakti certainly fills us completely. After it has filled us, setting the direction is the second principle. That energy needs a direction.","A great body of water has gathered in one place. A large reservoir has formed, water from the rain and, in other forms, water that has come from the mountains. However large that reservoir becomes, it must be given a direction. Otherwise, at any time, it can break its banks. There can be a flood. In whichever direction we send it, the Shakti flows that way.","There is a principle. Where attention goes, energy flows. If you have placed your attention outside, this Shakti goes outside. If you have turned your attention upward, it goes upward. If you are brooding, thinking, suffering — my whole life has gone this way, everyone is hurting me, I am alone — it flows in that direction, and all of it intensifies. In whatever direction we send it, the Shakti flows there. Where attention goes, energy flows. This must be set correctly.","We misuse a great deal of it without even knowing, through words, through actions, through thoughts, through our emotions. There are toxic emotions. Without our knowing, in those feelings, we keep wasting our energy, remaining in them. Through our patterns too it is wasted. Patterns mean certain events that keep repeating. We think we do not want them, and yet those situations keep coming. Not knowing how to deal with them, the pattern simply continues. The same pattern. If the direction is not set, the energy also goes that way, everything increases, and the same thing repeats. The Shakti must be put to right use."]$d9ens4json$::jsonb,
  3
