insert into public.sections (id, day_id, section_order, title, content, minutes)
select
  '4e8ca542-7120-4c4e-a591-85725cac8f1c'::uuid,
  d.id,
  5,
  $d9ens5title$The Third Principle · Knowledge, and the Work to Be Done$d9ens5title$,
  $d9ens5json$["The third principle. If it goes inward, if it remains inward and moves upward, this Shakti brings the attainment of knowledge. If it is kept outward, it brings success in the work. Through this Shakti, turned upward within, jnana siddhi. Gone outward, karya siddhi.","Hanuman had to wait even before Rama. He had come earlier, and from long before he was waiting for Rama. When the work of Rama came, the direction came. How mighty he is, how full of power. Hanuman means a bundle of energy, energy in full. Even as a child, taking the sun for a fruit, he thought he would eat it and nearly put it in his mouth. That is how powerful he is. But the work of Rama was needed. When he understood — this is the work I must do — because all of this is the life plan of so many, the plan of the soul. If we look at every episode of the Ramayana, the moment the work of Rama came, all the vanaras gathered in one place. Until then they were living in the ordinary way. Sugriva, Nila, and so many stalwarts, warriors. All of them are very strong, very powerful. Anjaneya is no ordinary being. They are very powerful. But the work of Rama — the moment that work came, his whole potential was released. Because there was a direction. That great work had to be accomplished. He could have done it alone. From here he flew, and in one leap he was there. He searched Lanka, found Mother Sita, recognised her, came back, and gave the whole report to Sri Rama. In the war of Rama and Ravana, through the whole Ramayana, the key role is Hanuman’s.","How great the work of Rama is. Sugriva has his role. Nila has his role. Jambavan has his role. All of them needed the work of Rama. There are many spiritual projects now. All of them are works like the work of Rama. Many great projects. They are not for one person to do. Rama could have done it alone. Rama has that much power. But that is not it. These are projects that everyone must do together. A great purpose. A great work. So, gone outward, there is success in the work. Remaining within us, the attainment of knowledge comes.","Both are important. Only when it goes upward within us does the attainment of knowledge come. If we have sent it downward, this energy can be misused. It should not be. When it goes upward, it reaches the Ajna chakra. The knowledge for which we take so many births can be known only while we are living on this earth, while we are in this body. After the body is left, all the knowledge is there. I am the Self. I have left the body. All of that is there. But we must come to know it here, with awareness, while we are in the body. That is the challenge.","So when the Shakti is within, it is the attainment of knowledge. When it has gone outward, a success in work comes to us through this Shakti. Direction is important. In the work to be done there are many kinds of work. Suppose we have placed most of our energy in worldly tasks. Some people are social butterflies. They are always giving parties. Always parties, always boasting, always talk. Everyone together, chatting, and they waste themselves in it. There is no useful talk in it. It is all talk of other people, of people who are not there. Always complaints. Complaints about someone. Judgements. When we speak of another person, we should never speak of someone who is absent in a negative way. Never. If you must speak, speak of their great qualities. There is at least one good quality. We must learn the art of appreciation. In every person there are good qualities. We must learn to appreciate them.","What is misused most is this socialising. Satsang is different. Satsang is not socialising. It has a great purpose. In satsang, everyone learns from everyone. They share all their experience. It creates a great field. So we must set our direction. It is very important. We must not misuse our energy. This is the third principle. If it goes inward, it is the attainment of knowledge. If it goes outward, it is success in the work. And we must also see for what kinds of work we should use our Shakti. We have taken this birth in order to do great work, as Hanuman did, and to leave having done great work. And within, we must gain that great knowledge, the knowledge of the Self."]$d9ens5json$::jsonb,
