insert into public.sections (id, day_id, section_order, title, content, minutes)
select
  '5baf2246-15a5-4b78-a0de-7f8ed0e25168'::uuid,
  d.id,
  6,
  $d9ens6title$The Fourth Principle · Where the Energy Leaks$d9ens6title$,
  $d9ens6json$["The fourth. Let us take an example, in a symbolic way. A water pipe is blocked. An obstruction has come. What happens there? All that water comes outside. It flows everywhere. Muddy water forms. Everything becomes a mess. We do not like it at all. It happens in our houses. Plumbing work. A plumber has to come and set it right. Within us, too, a great deal of plumbing is needed. We have many blocks in the Shakti.","Chiefly, because of our emotions, some problems come in giving this Shakti a direction. We are carrying chronic emotions. They are not from now. From childhood we have been clinging to one and the same thing. One emotion. One feeling. Let us say fear. That same fear. That same anger. That same sorrow. That same pain. That same depression.","The definition of emotion is energy in motion. Because there is an energy in emotion too. There is a great deal of energy in our feelings. There is a great deal of energy in our anger as well. The direction is different. It goes in another direction. A spiritual researcher set this out in the book Power versus Force, and published the whole inquiry there. It is a great inquiry. It is about measuring the units of these feelings, the units of energy and consciousness, through a test of applied kinesiology, through muscle testing. He discovered some great things. Each feeling has its own energy. Of all of them, gratitude has the greater energy. Gratitude has more units of consciousness. He researched this. We can observe it ourselves. When you are in joy, when you are living with a feeling of gratitude, how are your energy levels? How are your levels of consciousness? How are the levels of your Shakti and your Chaitanya? They are wonderful.","When we are in sorrow, when we are in fear, when a feeling of shame has come, when the feeling has come that I am less, how are our energy levels? As a balloon collapses when a hole comes in it, our energy collapses. Our units of energy are low. We can recognise this. Many of us do not know it. These emotions keep repeating. The same emotions. Through our awareness, through the meditation we are practising, we must be able to recognise these emotions. We must acknowledge them. We must not suppress them. We must not go and project them onto other people.","Many people do not know. They do not know how to deal with them. They suppress the emotions, or they go and project them. Rather than keep it inside, they go and scold someone else. They learned it that way from childhood. They do not know how to deal with these feelings. This is a great energy. There is a Shakti in each emotion. We must see what effect that emotion has on the Shakti. Some emotions deplete our units of energy. Chronic emotions mean what we have been carrying for a long time. Not this birth alone. We have been carrying the baggage of many births. We have brought a bundle. In it there is a great deal of fear. We are afraid of everything. Fear of losing our children. Fear of abandonment, the biggest fear. Everyone will leave me. I will be left alone. Fear of separation. Fear of not being approved. Fear of not being recognised. Or, I am weak. We are carrying so many, a bundle of many births. All of these keep depleting our Shakti.","Now we must recognise where our energy leaks. There is a water tank. A small hole is enough. From that small hole, drop by drop, the whole of it goes, and the tank becomes empty. This is very important. Where is our energy being misused? Where is it wasted? Where does it leak? Recognise it, and at once, with awareness, correct it.","When we understand the emotions rightly, through awareness, the direction is set. That anger itself turns into peace. The anger in us is one Shakti, expressed in many forms. The sorrow we are in, if we give it the direction of a great joy, becomes joy.","A situation has come. A family situation, a hard situation. A great pressure has come into you. You feel pressure. You feel stress. There are always quarrels at home. They quarrel with you. Whatever good you say, your feelings are all good, but everyone misunderstands you. Everything you say is a misunderstanding. Even if you trust, they misunderstand the trust. You think they are laughing at you in mockery. They are smiling in a friendly greeting, but you take them in another way. A situation has come. Many kinds of emotion can arise now. You may suffer. A hurt feeling may come. Why do they misunderstand me? This was not my intention. Why do they think of me wrongly? We suffer.","But some people take it in another way, from another point of view. This birth itself belongs to karma. Without a karma, this birth is not there. I have come to repay certain debts, whatever dues are there. In the family, that is all. The whole account is being cleared. Some people feel it that way. See the way they take it. Their angle of vision has changed, because they are meditating. They have gained Shakti. Chaitanya and knowledge are coming. The eye with which they see has changed. They have set the direction. In which direction does that Shakti go now? All the feelings go in a positive, uplifting direction.","Some emotions we call destructive. Some are constructive, feelings that build us. Love, joy, peace, gratitude, kindness, compassion, enthusiasm, optimism. All of these build us. They support us. They are life-enhancing, life-supporting emotions. Some feelings deplete our energy. They wear it down. They bring it to zero. In one anger, how much we lose. A person practises meditation for forty days. One situation. Anger came. You exploded like an atom bomb. That was all. The whole energy went. The Shakti of those forty days of meditation went. How many times this repeats.","All these emotions are in the subtle, in our mental field, in the field of feeling. If we do not recognise them properly, if we do not acknowledge them, if there is no awareness, if there is no understanding, all of them become blocks. In the field of feeling we make many interpretations. The angle from which we see situations is different. Seeing everything from a limited angle, understanding it as something limited, much fear comes, much sorrow, much pain. But a person of knowledge, a meditator, learns to interpret them in another way. He sees with another eye. If we see with the eye of knowledge, it is wonderful."]$d9ens6json$::jsonb,
  8
