insert into public.sections (id, day_id, section_order, title, content, minutes)
select
  '037670e1-d3aa-4dbe-a996-17d86f77b341'::uuid,
  d.id,
  8,
  $d9ens8title$Fully Appreciating Awareness$d9ens8title$,
  $d9ens8json$["This is called fully appreciating awareness. This is the eye of knowledge. With the eye of knowledge, everything becomes appreciation. If we can see every situation with a great eye of knowledge, in that very moment the places where this Shakti was obstructed, where the flow of Shakti was blocked, the energetic blockages in us, begin to clear.","For many people now there are blocks in the Anahata chakra, because they keep every single hurt here. They say, let me keep all the pain in the heart, and they keep it all in the heart. Rejection. Loss. They went away from me. A very severe pain has come. They keep it in the heart. There is a problem in the Anahata chakra. For some people it is a problem of expression, a problem of communication. For some, all the energy blockages are in the Manipura chakra. For some, in Svadhisthana. For some, in Muladhara.","When the eye of knowledge comes, wherever the energy is entangled, wherever the energy is not flowing, where a pipe has become blocked, the plumbing is done. Now we ourselves are that plumber. We are the plumber internally. We give the direction again. Seeing with the eye of knowledge, we unblock the energy that was emotionally entangled there. We remove it. It goes. That is why, while we are meditating, Shakti comes, and that Shakti flows strongly, a wonderful energy, a wonderful current. At a certain stage, first there is inner purification, purification of the field of the nadis. It certainly happens. It happens in every person. Only through this Shakti does the purification of the nadis happen. Only after this has happened do we cross Vishuddha and enter the Ajna chakra.","Vishuddha means a great purification, a special purity. Here a greater understanding happens. A power of great understanding comes in us. Each energy block that has formed in us must be finished in this purification of the nadis and the mind. Seeing with the eye of knowledge sets the direction. For many people, while the field of the nadis is being purified, much pain comes. The software of interpretation that is loaded here, the lens through which we see, makes us feel: what a great sinner I am, what wrongs we have done, how many karmas of wrong there are, when will I ever come out, perhaps I never will, I am a great sinner. We feel in this way. Our angle of vision makes that pain come severely. For some people, much pain comes in meditation. Much pain comes in the body, like labour pains, at the various chakras, at the places where the energy is blocked. Among the seventy-two thousand nadis, blocks can be anywhere, because each person’s life is different. Our challenges are different. Our situations are different. All those blocks are there.","We know what is happening inside, in our inner world. If we see with the eye of knowledge, the moment that knowledge has reached us, the moment the angle from which we see this block has changed, the block is cleared. Otherwise we stay stuck right there. A breeze of knowledge comes. We call it an insight. Looking outside, what comes is an external sight. Insight is what comes when we look into ourselves. An insight is a ray of knowledge, a great knowledge. We become able to see the situations of our life from another angle.","Suppose there is a building of seven floors. Seen from the ground floor, it is all right. Go to the first floor and look, and it is another way. The second floor. The third. We have gone up to the seventh floor. Seen from the seventh floor, from another angle, everything is very beautiful, and we appreciate it. We very much like to be in the penthouse. Many people like to go up and look. However high we keep looking, the angle of seeing from above is that vast, that wide. We are able to see that well. We call it the big picture. Or else it is a narrow picture. If we keep looking from a narrow, contracted feeling, from that angle, everything looks narrow. Everything looks like trouble. Everything looks like a problem. Seen from above, we gain that wonderful eye of knowledge.","Friends, we are speaking of the quality of tamas and the quality of rajas. In these Navaratri days, Mahishasura, Shumbha, Nishumbha, Chanda, Munda, Dhumralochana, Raktabija, and so many asuras. All of them are nothing but tamas and rajas. These defects are being expressed in many ways. That is all. The asuras are conceived here in symbolic form."]$d9ens8json$::jsonb,
