insert into public.sections (id, day_id, section_order, title, content, minutes)
select
  '8cfdca36-177f-47e5-a200-4e77bc8d2774'::uuid,
  d.id,
  9,
  $d9ens9title$Durgamasura and Shakambhari$d9ens9title$,
  $d9ens9json$["In the same way, we should also speak of another asura. His name is Durgamasura. Durgamasura too was full of tamas. It is said that he hid all the Vedas. He harmed them so that they were no longer with anyone. This must be understood in its symbolic form. Veda itself means knowledge. If there is no knowledge, there is only ignorance. Fear comes. Sorrow comes. The nature of knowledge is this. From knowledge comes joy. If we have gained knowledge, joy comes. If we have gained knowledge of the Self, the bliss of the Self comes. If we have gained the supreme knowledge, supreme bliss comes. If we have gained the knowledge of Brahman, the bliss of Brahman comes. As much knowledge as we have gained, that much joy. As much ignorance as there is, that much sorrow in our life.","This Durgamasura carried off all the Vedas. No one knew what he had done with them. Then what was the effect of Durgamasura on the earth? Famine came. Not one crop. Not one fruit. No plants. Nothing. Drought and calamity. Everyone was in sorrow. At that time, from this divine Shakti, from Mother Durga, she who is called Shakambhari took birth and came forth. Seeing this sorrow, tears came from her. We call it empathy. Someone speaks, and a response comes in us too. Seeing their difficulty, a response comes, and water flows from our eyes. For that Mother too, how dear children are. How much love, how much compassion. This love fell down in the form of tears. At once, vegetation came there. Branches, vegetables, fruits, and many great trees that give fruit. All of this came, and everyone was able to raise crops in plenty. The slaying of Durgamasura also took place. Many asuras are spoken of in this way.","In these Devi Navaratri days we read all of this. Ordinarily we keep telling them as stories. Vedavyasa has made all of this known to us, wonderfully, in symbolic form. A great symbolic language. All of this is not only the outer meaning. The inner meaning must be taken. It is all the victory over tamas and rajas. Sattva too must be crossed. The defect of sattva must also be crossed. Crossing these three qualities is the Navaratri practice that is taught here.","Only through the practice of meditation. Through the qualities of rajas and tamas, through these defects, there are many blockages in us now. There the Shakti leaks. It goes by a crooked path. The practice we are doing, meditation in particular, and this Navaratri practice too, is done intensely for this reason. By setting our own direction, there is success in the outer work, and inwardly there is the attainment of knowledge. In knowledge too there are many steps. Many attainments of knowledge. We must go from one level to another. Knowledge too is endless, and we must keep learning it."]$d9ens9json$::jsonb,
