insert into public.sections (id, day_id, section_order, title, content, minutes)
select
  '5ff676eb-5cfc-4077-a5ff-4c267fa11e2c'::uuid,
  d.id,
  10,
  $d9ens10title$Mother Nature, and Our Own Mother$d9ens10title$,
  $d9ens10json$["Friends, yesterday we spoke of this Prakriti, of Mother Nature. That divine Shakti appears to us here as Mother Nature. We should not see this Nature merely as nature. We should feel this Nature as the reality of the Supreme. The Mother of the world has filled this whole creation, as this tree, as the animals. We must be able to see with that feeling. We said it yesterday. However close our bond with our own mother is, that close we are able to go to the Mother of the world. We are able to take that Shakti to that extent. That connection is formed. The connection with Mother Devi, with that Shakti, with Mother Durga, is built in us.","How can we receive that Shakti? The feeling we have when we are near our own mother is the same feeling toward this Shakti. What is in the gross is also within. What is outside is also within. What is in the gross world is also happening in the subtle world. It is the same in the causal world.","That is why there is a question for all of us. It is about our bond with our mother. Suppose your mother is near you now. She may be in the body, or she may have left the body. If you think once about your connection with her, with your biological mother, how much distance is there between the two of you? Do you feel very close to her, or is she very far, and are you unable to connect? What are your judgements? There are many judgements of our mother. We judge her a great deal. Where there is judgement, we become separate. We go far. If we do not accept even this mother, where else will we accept that mother, the Mother of the world? First we must be able to accept this mother, our own mother.","Wherever there is a block, you feel a great distance between you and Amma. It is an emotional distance. Physically you may be in the same house. You may be speaking, and speaking well. But inside, you and your mother feel far, very far. It is not about the physical distance. Many people are very near. They speak every day. They meet every day. They live in the same house. You live with your mother. And still a great distance from Amma comes over you."]$d9ens10json$::jsonb,
