insert into public.sections (id, day_id, section_order, title, content, minutes)
select
  '2fb1f597-dfed-4ad4-a719-7e8ba845b1a1'::uuid,
  d.id,
  15,
  $d9ens15title$Questions · Pilgrimage and the Journey Within$d9ens15title$,
  $d9ens15json$["Thank you. Wonderful, friends. Let us take a few sharings. Last, Sri Lakshmi spoke. Thank you, Sir, for giving me the chance. I am connecting on YouTube today. I came into Zoom only today. I have also come to Quantum Life University once, and I met you once. I also took a personal session with Harika Madam. It was very good. I am still doing what Madam taught, and I am also clearing my emotional blockages.","I have a question. You once said that if we place our attention on the breath, liberation comes in the subtle. That settled in me so deeply. After that, many times, a chance came to go with some friends on the Char Dham, and to Manasarovar. But what I felt was this. Liberation is here. When Shiva and Shakti are within us, is there a need for us to go all the way there? You also said that we should connect with the energies by going to the great Shakti pithas, by going on such a pilgrimage. Sir, I have a doubt. If we stay at home and do this practice, if we keep connecting with our own Shakti, how necessary is that?","Very good, Madam. You have asked a good question, because many people have this doubt. Many people keep going on pilgrimages. A great many pilgrimages. There is nothing wrong in saying, go and bathe in the Ganga. If one is able to go, if it feels right, if all the means are there, one may go and do all of it. But the greater practices must be done there. One must meditate. And without going on any pilgrimage, staying in our own house, everything is available. This inner pilgrimage is a journey we make within. On this journey too, everything comes to us wonderfully.","Once, the whole war was over. The Mahabharata war was finished. The Pandavas planned a pilgrimage. Krishna is their kin, the Supreme. They invited him too. Please come on the pilgrimage. Krishna said: I have many appointments. I have some commitments. You go. But I will give you one thing as my symbol. I will give you a bottle gourd. Take the gourd with you. Wherever you go on this pilgrimage, immerse this too in the river, and bring it back. Their journey was forty days. After forty days they would return. Bring it back, he said. Wherever you worship, place the gourd there. Do it feeling that I myself am there. They did exactly this. They went, taking the gourd. They immersed it everywhere as Krishna. Wherever there was worship in the temples, wherever there was practice, they placed it there too.","Then they came back. Dharmaraja asked: Krishna, what should we do now? What will you do with the gourd? He said: cook a meal for everyone. Invite everyone in the town, and serve them a proper meal. They made sambar with that gourd. They cooked. And everyone vomited. All the Pandavas asked, how did it happen like this? This gourd came with us on the pilgrimage. It is sacred. Why has it made everyone vomit? When they went to Krishna to report, he was laughing. In that very laughter they understood. Through the pilgrimages, nothing changed even in the gourd. What change comes in a person? People wander about outside. They go here and they go there. When they bathe in the Ganga, the sins do not leave. However many bathe, nothing happens. All those ghosts called sins stay right there, and catch hold of them again.","There is nothing wrong in it. If one is able to go, it is excellent to go and practise. The main thing is the practice. For this great meditation there are fine experiments. It can be done sitting in our own house. Liberation in the subtle. We said this one day. This very body is the city of Kashi. This is Manasarovar. This is Mount Kailasa. Every Jyotirlinga is within us. Every place of Shakti is within us. And these outer places should not be made less of either. They are wonderful. Once, we were taking classes in Tamil Nadu. There I heard of Mother Kamakshi of Kanchi, and I felt I must go. We went to Kanchi. Adi Shankaracharya also did a process there. The divine Shakti in that place was so intense that people could not bear it. He made a shield. In many places he lessened the intensity of that Shakti for everyone and made a shield. Only sadhakas are able to receive it.","When we go there, we practise in the ordinary way. The moment we sat down in meditation, the Shakti was such that she appeared in the form of the Mother. She came together with a parrot. There is a parrot. She came with the parrot as her vehicle. She came seated on the parrot, a great form, and she asked me to sit with her too. This is an experience of knowledge. It is an experience that happened in the subtle. We should understand it as a symbol, in its symbolic form. She showed many things. It was a wonderful experience. After that, when the eyes were opened, I had never known much about her. A longing arose to know a little. We came out and were looking at everything. There are parrots everywhere there. There are many parrots in that temple. Then, coming outside, all the pictures were visible. In all those pictures there is a parrot beside her. Then I read her book. It is written there that sages and yogis remain near her in the form of parrots, near the Mother of the world, near Mother Kamakshi of Kanchi. I did not know this. I did not know that the parrot is her vehicle. I did not know that the parrots are there. But experiences of this kind do happen.","Whenever one goes, these great and wonderful fields of Shakti — Srisailam, where the Mother of the world is present as two, in the reality of Ardhanarishvara — and so it is in many places. All of this is wonderful. If one can go, it is wonderful. But all of this is also within us, inwardly, in the subtle. Everything is there. We must not forget this and do only the other. It will not do. We must gain this within.","Lakshmi said: when we go, we should meditate there and connect with the energies. If we meditate, that is enough. We should sit in a state free of thought, in inner silence. The vibration that is there, that whole field, helps us. The meditation we do ordinarily and the meditation we do in a pyramid are different. The Shakti is different, a wonderful Shakti. A pyramid itself is the Sri Chakra. A pyramid itself is Mount Meru. It is like meditating upon Mount Meru. A temple is the same. All of these are places of Shakti. In every temple there is a prana pratishtha. There is a great architecture. There is a sacred geometry. The sanctum itself is in the form of a pyramid. There is a wonderful science behind this. When you go, meditate well. Sit in a state free of thought. That is all. There is no need to visualise the form of the deity. Whatever is meant to come in that place will come to us. Experiences will be given. All the best.","She asked one more thing. On the 24th and 25th there is a workshop for doctors. May Ayurvedic physicians also come? Ayurveda, naturopathy, acupuncture — anyone may come. Anyone. Because we want the many people who are in the medical field to know this approach as well. Spiritual birth, pregnancy. There are so many caesareans, so many kinds. This method, from the spiritual angle too, spiritual healing. It is in order to give them this understanding that we are holding these two days for them. So invite all of them. They may come. Thank you.","A chance was then given to those who are new, who have never spoken. Vanajakshi garu, please speak now. Namaskaram, Sir. Namaskaram, Madam. Your hand is in the way, and you are not visible. Please come a little nearer to the camera. Now you are visible. Vanajakshi, please tell us.","She said: we come for meditation. I am doing it every day. My attention itself is on meditation. I like it very much. Today I wanted to speak with you, and with my son beside me. Very good, Amma. You said you like meditation very much. Those who like it are very dear to Sri Krishna. And then, very dear to the Mother of the world. Whoever is in meditation, whoever practises meditation, is, it is said, very dear to Shiva. How much you like it. You are practising so well. Wonderful, Amma. Thank you. All the best."]$d9ens15json$::jsonb,
  11
