insert into public.sections (id, day_id, section_order, title, content, minutes)
select
  '91f489b0-e760-4c97-a7cf-a58d06f2300b'::uuid,
  d.id,
  16,
  $d9ens16title$Questions · Health and a Repeating Illness$d9ens16title$,
  $d9ens16json$["Prarthana garu. Namaste, Sir. Good morning. Happy Navaratri. Thank you, Amma. One question. I am actually in the practice of meditation. I am doing it all well. Even so, health issues keep coming repeatedly. You said that health is a lesson. But I am not able to understand what lesson it has come to teach.","Some karmas are long-standing. We should know that whatever has been troubling us for a long time belongs to karma. Karmas are lessons. We have understood karma as training. They are not there to punish us. They are not there to hurt us. They are training. What is to be learned from them must be learned. They teach us certain things. Until we have learned them, we must be patient for a while. The feeling to hold is this. Whatever is there is being washed away. It is leaving me. I let go. Whatever belonged to a past birth, whatever had grown large, is leaving through these symptoms. Then let your whole attention be a focus on joy. Practise joy. Be joyful in every moment. To live contented, we must remain immersed in that every moment. Be aware every moment. Keep practising it, Amma.","She said: for two years I am well, and every two years it returns. For girls there is the menstrual cycle, and there is PCOD. I am suffering in that matter. You should address this a little further with someone’s help, in the way of counselling. These are matters of the feminine. There are blind spots. We cannot see some things ourselves. Which lessons they are. When others, seniors, hold the space, when the stage is held, we become able to recognise them. Take that help and support. Wonderful, Prarthana garu. Thank you."]$d9ens16json$::jsonb,
  2
