insert into public.sections (id, day_id, section_order, title, content, minutes)
select
  'a885e064-2de2-4c67-a1ef-9f14a9c9dbb5'::uuid,
  d.id,
  1,
  $d10ens1title$Divine Feminine Energy and Self-Knowledge$d10ens1title$,
  $d10ens1json$["Good morning, wonderful friends of Jnanodayam. During these nine days, we have been learning about Shakti, the Divine Mother's energy that pervades everything. Knowing about energy and directly knowing energy are different things. Knowing about Self-knowledge and actually knowing the Self are different. Knowing about truth and directly realizing truth are different. When we say “about,” we enter analysis, examination, and theory. What matters is practice. During the rainy season, conditions favor the growth of crops, and farmers know to sow their seeds then. Likewise, during Navaratri, the flow of energy is especially favorable. That is why Navaratri and Dasara are great festivals for meditators and spiritual practitioners.","All these observances exist for spiritual practice. We have now reached the tenth day, Vijayadashami, after the nine nights of Navaratri. What is the inner meaning of this festival? Without understanding its meaning, we merely perform ceremonies and rituals because our ancestors performed them. We should understand why we celebrate Vijayadashami. Every day we have been learning about Shakti and how to experience it directly. Yesterday we discussed seven principles. The first is that we receive energy through meditation.","There is energy throughout nature, and we receive it in other ways too. Listening to good music and uplifting sounds gives energy. Food also gives energy; that is its very purpose. We receive energy through the five senses. But meditation is the principal and most important means of receiving universal energy. As energy fills us and we become embodiments of energy, we begin to recognize consciousness. At first, energy and consciousness seem separate, but in truth they are one. They are never separate; they are two expressions of the same reality. Please understand this point carefully.","Energy and consciousness may appear different. When Kundalini Shakti rises upward and reaches consciousness, their oneness is realized. This is the principle of Ardhanarishvara: Mother Parvati and Shiva are not two but one. The knowledge born of their union is also one. Energy, consciousness, and the knowledge arising from their union—these three are experienced by every sincere meditator. Under the favorable conditions of Navaratri, we absorb abundant universal energy. Through energy we recognize consciousness, and through their union we gain knowledge. Our entire journey and practice are for Self-knowledge: Who am I? What should I do? What is my purpose? We must not misuse the energy awakened by our practice.","Universal energy, Kundalini energy, and the energy hidden within us must be used for great work. Hanuman used his strength in service of Rama's mission. We too need a grand purpose. This is the second principle. Our energy leaks away in many ways and is often misused. We must learn to contain it, as water is held in a reservoir, and then direct it toward our highest goal and its fulfillment.","The third point we discussed yesterday was that awakened energy takes two directions: inward and outward. When directed inward, we associate it with the feminine principle, feminine energy. When expressed in the external world, it manifests as masculine energy."]$d10ens1json$::jsonb,
  4
