insert into public.sections (id, day_id, section_order, title, content, minutes)
select
  'c08106d8-82b1-418a-ab0f-fdee69222690'::uuid,
  d.id,
  5,
  $d10ens5title$Wisdom, Self-Reflection, and the Meaning of Victory$d10ens5title$,
  $d10ens5json$["They observed and acknowledged their anger and other emotions with awareness. They did not merely suppress them; they waited for the right expression and the right time. They turned every failure into strength.","They transformed curses into blessings. An enlightened meditator turns every curse into a blessing; an unenlightened person may turn even a blessing into a curse. Through the vision of wisdom and a change in perception, a meditator can transform even an unbearable situation. For the Pandavas, twelve years in the forest and one year incognito were transformative. It was as if they had taken a second birth within the same lifetime: they became dvijas, twice-born, through self-realization and self-regeneration. On Vijayadashami, let us ask: What is our first victory? What is the very first success in our lives?","Please type your answer in the chat. Harika madam answered, “Being born.” Correct! Other things may be victories, but birth is the first victory. It began in the mother's womb. In this spiritual view, countless souls await an opportunity to incarnate; you were given the opportunity and chose your mother, father, and family as part of your divine plan. At the biological level, among countless sperm cells, only one fertilizes the ovum.","Of the countless souls, you received the opportunity to come to Earth. You faced the conditions of the womb and were born. Being born is your first victory, and it is also a great victory for your mother. Pregnancy might have ended in miscarriage, or the baby might not have survived after birth. But you arrived. The mother is an expression of Jagannmata, the Divine Mother, and has fulfilled the great role of bringing a divine soul into an earthly body. It is a victory for both mother and child. Now what is the final victory? Is it becoming a billionaire, gaining a position, or winning a Nobel Prize? Someone answered “conscious death.” Kings once thought conquering a kingdom was victory, but true victory is conquering ourselves. Knowing ourselves, attaining Atma Jnana and Brahma Jnana—these are the highest, ultimate successes. Our first victory begins with our mother; our final victory is fulfilled through the Divine Mother.","That final victory comes with the help of Jagannmata and Divine Shakti. On Vijayadashami, let us discuss a few principles. First is the principle of self-confidence. We often underestimate ourselves; that is great ignorance. The first step to victory is believing that the power of the Divine Mother herself lies within you. Many suffer from inferiority, fear, and a lack of complete faith in themselves. They believe others are great but do not see their own greatness. Everyone has greatness within. Some say, “I cannot meditate as well as others. They are wise masters, but I am not.” Yet we are all masters. Self-belief, self-confidence, self-worth, and self-esteem are the first steps. Many people undertake projects and work toward goals."]$d10ens5json$::jsonb,
