insert into public.sections (id, day_id, section_order, title, content, minutes)
select
  '836b77c2-7879-4954-a2b0-6595206dfd01'::uuid,
  d.id,
  7,
  $d10ens7title$Self-Knowledge and a Vision for Life$d10ens7title$,
  $d10ens7json$["Aparajita means the power that is undefeated, the state of no defeat. The Pandavas held that feeling of “no failure.” On Vijayadashami, remember that our first success came through our mother, while our ultimate success comes through knowing ourselves. We discover our energy and gain the wisdom arising from the union of energy and consciousness. Conscious death and other attainments are fruits of how we live. Those who become masters of their inner world and gain wisdom through direct experience live wonderfully in the outer world as well.","Whatever we undertake on Vijayadashami, let us begin with a strong connection to the infinite energy present within ourselves and everyone. We should act with the conviction that we can use that energy to accomplish our task. The beginning matters most. The first step leads to a thousand steps, yet we hesitate at the first step, asking, “Can I climb? Can I do it? Will it work?” Today we should recognize and remove self-doubt.","Wonderful friends, we have observed Navaratri beautifully and entered energetic states. But practice does not end today. We were more attentive during these favorable days; afterward we should still meditate for an hour every day. Our sadhana must be continuous, both inwardly and outwardly. Inward practice is meditation; outward practice is the way we live, the situations we face, and the people with whom we interact. Everything in life can become sadhana. Today let us do a small exercise concerning real success. To succeed, we must not doubt whether our goal will be attained. If our goal is Self-knowledge, it brings inner bliss and peace and benefits our outer life as well.","We must remove self-doubt and become inwardly what we wish to attain. Imagine the feeling you would have if your project or goal were already accomplished, and feel that feeling now. Whatever your profession, see yourself as successful in it. That future possibility already exists subtly within you like a seed. The doubting mind—the “Doubting Thomas” mind—keeps blocking it.","Thoughts such as “It may be difficult,” “I may fail,” and “I will do it later” hold us back. Such negativity and postponement are expressions of tamoguna. We should experience our highest possibility right now, in this present moment, as if we had already become it. For example, you may be like a drop of water, while your highest possibility is the vast ocean. That possibility exists within you; someday you will realize it.","Even while you are a tiny drop, feel yourself to be the ocean now. The entire ocean is hidden within the drop."]$d10ens7json$::jsonb,
