insert into public.sections (id, day_id, section_order, title, content, minutes)
select
  '09f25e6f-430d-4207-a84b-5f5aa0460f68'::uuid,
  d.id,
  8,
  $d10ens8title$Transformation Through Practice$d10ens8title$,
  $d10ens8json$["Suppose you currently teach meditation to one hundred people a day, but your goal in this lifetime is to teach ten million people. Through meditation, they may experience inner transformation, joy, and wisdom. Is teaching ten million people possible? That future already exists in subtle seed form as a possibility. Feel it now. See yourself on the day when your goal has been fulfilled.","Imagine that you have taught meditation to ten million people, inspired them toward a vegetarian way of life, and helped organize ten million meditation yajnas. Imagine these great achievements and connect now with your highest possibility. Friends, let us close our eyes for a short four-minute process on this auspicious Vijayadashami. Let us attune ourselves to the victory we wish to attain. Connect with the breath, observe inhalation and exhalation, and quiet the mind. Remember that our mother gave us our first victory by bringing us into this world. Our relationship with our mother is our first successful relationship. Let us thank her.","Recognize our mother as the source of that first victory. Feel gratitude fully. Now picture yourself in the future, having accomplished a meaningful goal. It may be Self-knowledge, a project, a talent, or an expression of creativity. Feel now what your future self would feel on achieving that success.","In your subtle inner world, visualize yourself fully developed, with your full potential awakened, victorious inwardly and outwardly. Experience now the feeling of that future day. Observe your future self, and allow that future self and your present self to become one in this moment.","Set aside self-doubt and feelings such as “I am worthless,” “I am unworthy,” “I am inadequate,” and “I am not good enough.” Put aside doubts about whether the goal will happen. Tune fully into the experience of success. Some feel joy; others feel peace, completeness, fulfillment, or the sense that life has become meaningful. Whatever that feeling is, experience it now in your body. Breathe gently and remain in it for a minute. “I am victorious; there is no defeat for me.” Slowly open your eyes with a peaceful smile.","There is only success, no failure. From today, let us erase the word “failure” from our dictionary. One success leads to another, and then another, both inwardly and outwardly. Take your time opening your eyes, dear friends. May you be victorious; may you achieve great victory. Blessings to you all. Wonderful friends, let us now celebrate Vijayadashami by listening to a beautiful song from Harika madam."]$d10ens8json$::jsonb,
