insert into public.sections (id, day_id, section_order, title, content, minutes)
select
  'd566d981-8e51-42ea-acaa-540f2b40404b'::uuid,
  d.id,
  9,
  $d10ens9title$Self-Awareness and Participant Reflections$d10ens9title$,
  $d10ens9json$["[A chanting-only performance of the Durga Sukta by Harika is omitted.] Wonderful, Harika madam. You offered everyone such a beautiful chant for Vijayadashami. Thank you. Let us now hear from participants, including some who have been waiting since yesterday and some who are new. First is Sandhya, whose birthday is today.","Sandhya: Namaste, sir. Through these Jnanodayam classes you are giving us so much wisdom. Earlier I kept struggling, thinking, “I do not have this or that,” and searching for reasons. Now I do not even feel the need to ask those questions. Everything is there. Through practice, we must search inwardly. I was searching outside for causes and could not find them; today you explained that we should look within. The Mother's energy is infinite. When I was not connected with her, I behaved as though I knew everything and made mistakes without understanding. Today I ask her forgiveness. I seek your blessings so that this wisdom becomes firmly established within me. You have said in earlier classes that Ganesha is at Muladhara, that Mother and Father are within us, that Shanmukha is within us, that Sita is at Muladhara and Rama at Sahasrara, and that we must hold on to the breath, Hanuman. I did not understand how precious the breath was and kept running here and there. Now I am learning to sit. I feel good simply sitting; I no longer feel like going anywhere. I wish to begin this inward journey, and I ask for your blessings.","Teacher: Wonderful, Sandhya madam. Happy birthday. Thank you to your parents. I wish you wonderful spiritual growth and the attainment of great states of the Self through meditation. Thank you also for making a donation to Quantum Life University programs on your birthday.","Ashwini and Narasimha: Namaste, sir. Happy Dasara. From these nine days of classes I have learned a great deal. I am listening to the classes and attending workshops. When you explained the subtle qualities within us, I began observing them during meditation over the last four days. After the Eckhart Tolle book series, I have been reading the book again and putting it into practice. I practice not only in meditation but in ordinary daily life. I notice that I still think about the past; such thoughts arise without my knowing. I am applying what I learned even outside my regular meditation. Thank you.","Teacher: Wonderful. Thank you for sharing. A question from Sushmita in the YouTube chat asks: What is Vipassana meditation? How is it different from Anapanasati, and which is better? They are not two competing things. The starting point is always Anapanasati, awareness of the breath. Through that practice, the state or experience of Vipassana arises. Buddha first taught everyone to begin with Anapanasati."]$d10ens9json$::jsonb,
