insert into public.sections (id, day_id, section_order, title, content, minutes)
select
  'c3f8f65c-a6d1-4848-a335-867cd5bf9c47'::uuid,
  d.id,
  10,
  $d10ens10title$Dasara Message and Questions and Answers$d10ens10title$,
  $d10ens10json$["The Buddha explained how to observe inhalation and exhalation. Then come states described as kayanupassana, vedananupassana, cittanupassana, and dhammanupassana. These are experiences and stages of observation. Vipassana is seeing in a special, clear way—seeing truth as truth and falsehood as falsehood. Beyond that lies the state of nirvana. These are logical, sequential steps, one after another. Do not be confused: meditation begins with awareness of inhalation and exhalation. Vipassana is a fruit of that practice. Through practice, many experiences, including those associated with the third eye, may arise.","The host invites Usha Sayani to speak, but she initially has difficulty unmuting. The host asks her to accept the request or click the blue unmute button and says they will return to her. Meanwhile, Mitra Ramadevi is invited to share.","Ramadevi: Namaste, sir. My heartfelt salutations to Patriji, Patriji madam, you, Lakshmi madam, and the QLU community. Happy Dasara to everyone. I have been meditating every day during Navaratri. Your classes have been wonderful. We meditate from 9 p.m. to 5 a.m. at night and another two hours at the center in the afternoon—ten hours a day. We hardly sleep, yet we feel healthy and active and continue our work. We hold meditation sessions at a different person's house each day. In meditation, I experience myself as a complete soul, connected with the Divine Mother, like a little child in her lap. Today, while meditating in a room, I saw a large tiger sitting in front of me. Someone came and asked how I could sit in a room with a tiger. I replied that I had been sitting there looking at it for three hours.","I feel great joy. This Navaratri meditation has been extraordinary, and I am learning much wisdom from your classes. I now believe I will achieve my goal: to establish a meditation center with a pyramid where thousands or lakhs of people can sit, meditate, gain wisdom, receive the nectar of meditation, and leave healthy and happy. I have the firm confidence that I will complete this goal in this lifetime. I feel that through practice what I intend can happen. Thank you for giving me this opportunity.","Teacher: Thank you, Ramadevi madam. You described your experiences beautifully.","Usha: Namaste, sir. Dasara greetings to you, Lakshmi madam, Harika madam, and everyone here. I am very happy today. In these nine days, I learned that the many qualities represented by the demons exist within us and how to remove them. Earlier I knew only that the Goddess killed demons; I did not understand their inner meaning. I have experienced some transformation. When difficulties arose at home, I learned to accept them and work through them. From the tenth through the thirty-first, we have organized twenty-one days of twelve-hour meditation sessions, held in different homes. We are all participating, experiencing the energy and putting into practice what you teach each morning. I feel the Divine Mother is giving me the strength to practice this wisdom. I am deeply grateful. Please visit the Trimurti Pyramid Meditation Center at Meerpet; we invite you. Thank you.","Teacher: Wonderful. Your continuous meditation program is excellent.","Venkateswarulu: Namaste, sir. Happy Vijayadashami to everyone in the group and to your family. I received so much knowledge through these nine days. I understood that everything is in Mother Earth and the Divine Mother and that we should connect with her. I spent more time meditating this year. Though I am far away, I feel fortunate to receive this wisdom through you. My wife also meditates, and meditation is a part of our daily life. Jnanodayam has been very useful in my life. Thank you for allowing me to speak.","Teacher: Thank you, Venkateswarulu. Wonderful. Next, Venkata Lakshmi Devi; let us all keep our sharing brief."]$d10ens10json$::jsonb,
